1
00:02:04,271 --> 00:02:08,531
NO ANIMALS WERE HURT DURING
THE PRODUCTION OF THIS SHOW

2
00:02:09,348 --> 00:02:13,559
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:17,402 --> 00:02:22,052
I'll find you in the afterlife
if you die before killing 5 cruels!

4
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:26,300
Come on!
Do your job, valiants!

5
00:02:29,644 --> 00:02:32,864
For my brother Goktug!
Allah is eternal!

6
00:02:32,988 --> 00:02:34,768
Allah is righteous!

7
00:02:59,535 --> 00:03:02,275
You irrigated
the soil with my brother's blood!

8
00:03:02,396 --> 00:03:05,116
The soil is haram for you now!

9
00:04:37,494 --> 00:04:40,444
Soldiers!
Remove the carriage!

10
00:04:41,069 --> 00:04:42,619
Fast!

11
00:04:49,815 --> 00:04:51,265
Fast!

12
00:05:00,196 --> 00:05:01,687
Turgut!

13
00:05:01,687 --> 00:05:03,617
Kosses!

14
00:05:05,629 --> 00:05:07,399
Traitor Kosses!

15
00:05:07,551 --> 00:05:10,131
We can't hang on here too long,
Turgut Bey.

16
00:05:10,706 --> 00:05:12,066
What's the plan?

17
00:05:12,210 --> 00:05:14,030
We'll figure it out.

18
00:05:25,579 --> 00:05:27,546
Kutan!
Serhan!

19
00:05:27,546 --> 00:05:29,416
Take the shields to the carriage!

20
00:05:41,056 --> 00:05:42,486
Arrows!

21
00:05:43,402 --> 00:05:45,592
Faster!
Faster!

22
00:05:49,019 --> 00:05:51,229
You surprised me, Turgut Bey.

23
00:05:51,737 --> 00:05:55,737
I have never thought
I would be saved by you.

24
00:05:55,863 --> 00:05:58,033
It's too early to tell, Kosses.

25
00:05:58,207 --> 00:06:01,347
We'll talk once we get rid of them.

26
00:06:21,472 --> 00:06:23,112
Kosses, shield!

27
00:06:23,141 --> 00:06:24,481
Here!

28
00:06:35,268 --> 00:06:39,178
The traitor and the shepherd
are running away! Catch them!

29
00:06:39,514 --> 00:06:40,894
Fast!

30
00:06:42,224 --> 00:06:43,904
Fast!

31
00:07:02,105 --> 00:07:06,311
I want both the shepherd
and traitor Kosses!

32
00:07:06,311 --> 00:07:09,181
Right now!
Follow them!

33
00:07:22,183 --> 00:07:24,793
You are very stubborn, Osman.

34
00:07:24,934 --> 00:07:28,904
But you are going to die eventually.

35
00:08:17,306 --> 00:08:18,906
Alps, stop.

36
00:08:19,692 --> 00:08:21,372
We need to split up.

37
00:08:22,117 --> 00:08:26,928
Split now so that they divide
and get confused.

38
00:08:27,528 --> 00:08:31,308
Then we'll meet in Baspinar,
Inshallah (I hope)

39
00:08:31,396 --> 00:08:33,056
Inshallah (I hope so), my Bey.

40
00:08:33,191 --> 00:08:35,681
Kosses, go with them.

41
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,330
I'll be behind you.

42
00:08:38,330 --> 00:08:40,799
No Turgut Bey.
I can't leave you.

43
00:08:40,866 --> 00:08:44,676
We should go different ways so
they divide.

44
00:08:45,239 --> 00:08:47,299
We'll have a higher chance to survive.

45
00:08:48,564 --> 00:08:50,794
There is no time, Kosses.
Go now.

46
00:08:51,827 --> 00:08:53,267
Okay.

47
00:08:53,362 --> 00:08:55,502
Let's go Alps!

48
00:10:29,723 --> 00:10:31,163
You are...

49
00:10:31,247 --> 00:10:33,577
...like a galloper...

50
00:10:34,284 --> 00:10:35,574
...in this land.

51
00:10:41,693 --> 00:10:45,293
“I bear witness that there is no God
but Allah...

52
00:10:47,019 --> 00:10:51,519
...and I bear witness that Muhammad is...

53
00:10:53,063 --> 00:10:54,743
...the messenger of Allah”.

54
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,462
Turgut Bey!

55
00:11:37,884 --> 00:11:39,904
Are you late for somewhere?

56
00:11:40,343 --> 00:11:43,023
We have an unfinished talk.

57
00:11:43,168 --> 00:11:44,918
You are coward.

58
00:11:45,706 --> 00:11:47,956
You are so afraid of me that...

59
00:11:48,544 --> 00:11:52,244
...you do not face me alone.
You brought your dogs.

60
00:11:53,648 --> 00:11:55,772
Turgut, Turgut.

61
00:11:55,772 --> 00:11:57,842
You care about yourself a lot.

62
00:11:59,209 --> 00:12:02,025
You are someone I'll just crush
for me.

63
00:12:02,025 --> 00:12:04,955
You exceeded your limits,
I got angry.

64
00:12:04,961 --> 00:12:07,301
That's all.
I mean that's all!

65
00:12:10,366 --> 00:12:12,426
Come on now.

66
00:12:39,770 --> 00:12:41,960
Yes, Turgut Bey.

67
00:12:42,514 --> 00:12:46,924
As you see, I am standing,
you are down.

68
00:12:47,022 --> 00:12:50,702
I am at the peak,
you are at the bottom.

69
00:12:50,925 --> 00:12:53,595
You are not any different
from a snake, Nikola.

70
00:12:53,767 --> 00:12:57,967
You can only crawl onto a peak.

71
00:12:59,068 --> 00:13:00,958
I am an eagle.

72
00:13:01,916 --> 00:13:05,096
Even if I fall, I fall while flying.

73
00:13:06,706 --> 00:13:09,826
Those are too fancy sentences
for a shepherd, Turgut Bey.

74
00:13:10,026 --> 00:13:12,206
Bravo, Bravo.

75
00:13:15,614 --> 00:13:19,664
If you are an eagle,
and your wings are broken...

76
00:13:20,683 --> 00:13:23,753
...and if you are alone, Turgut Bey...

77
00:13:24,441 --> 00:13:28,271
...that snake will eat you.

78
00:13:29,827 --> 00:13:32,357
This is your end.

79
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:41,182
This is your time to die, Turgut Bey.

80
00:13:41,758 --> 00:13:44,708
Even if we die, we become a martyr.

81
00:13:45,129 --> 00:13:48,009
We are not regretful.
We don't care about the mortal life.

82
00:13:49,629 --> 00:13:52,299
Only Mari...

83
00:13:55,062 --> 00:13:58,572
...she is my heart, she is my Hatun.

84
00:14:04,155 --> 00:14:06,065
Only that fact hurts me.

85
00:14:08,357 --> 00:14:11,317
There is nothing else.
Do what you are going to do now.

86
00:14:15,848 --> 00:14:18,218
Honorless Nikola!

87
00:14:18,674 --> 00:14:21,364
The ignoble who backstabbed me!

88
00:14:21,557 --> 00:14:23,527
Did you think I wouldn't go after you?

89
00:14:32,489 --> 00:14:34,059
Kosses!

90
00:14:34,111 --> 00:14:36,071
Traitor Kosses!

91
00:14:37,567 --> 00:14:41,992
I wouldn't want to kill Turgut and
leave you alive anyway!

92
00:14:41,992 --> 00:14:43,692
I am glad to have you here.

93
00:14:49,929 --> 00:14:53,089
I am aware of your evil plans,
you low dog!

94
00:14:53,271 --> 00:14:56,511
Harmankaya Castle is too large for you,
do you hear me?!

95
00:14:58,376 --> 00:15:01,606
I told you not to come after me,
but it's a good thing you did.

96
00:15:01,712 --> 00:15:05,692
Yeah, but how was I supposed to explain
myself If I went back to Mari without you?

97
00:15:05,692 --> 00:15:08,206
Let's get out of here!
Come on, soldiers!

98
00:15:30,255 --> 00:15:31,945
- Damn it!
- Sir?

99
00:15:32,048 --> 00:15:33,908
Go after them, Argus!

100
00:15:33,984 --> 00:15:35,884
I cannot leave you like this!

101
00:15:36,144 --> 00:15:38,264
Argus, go after them!

102
00:15:39,463 --> 00:15:42,953
Forgive me, sir, I can't leave you.

103
00:16:10,474 --> 00:16:14,774
Osman is a great bey...

104
00:16:15,356 --> 00:16:17,456
...he should not die like this...

105
00:16:18,921 --> 00:16:21,181
He won't die on the battlefield...

106
00:16:22,277 --> 00:16:24,377
Your reputation will not live on.

107
00:16:27,201 --> 00:16:28,691
Mingiyan...

108
00:16:30,009 --> 00:16:33,499
He will be crushed under the horses...

109
00:16:33,808 --> 00:16:35,878
...like a traitor,...

110
00:17:10,755 --> 00:17:14,405
...no one will be sorry for Osman...

111
00:17:16,352 --> 00:17:20,722
He will beg for not living
the things he has lived.

112
00:17:21,309 --> 00:17:24,589
I will submit you to Erlik Khan.

113
00:17:26,089 --> 00:17:29,359
I will beg Gök Tengri.

114
00:17:31,022 --> 00:17:36,182
Everyone will know that Geyhatun has come.

115
00:17:49,428 --> 00:17:51,998
The tribe already has a bey.

116
00:17:52,569 --> 00:17:56,869
Beylik feast will not be arranged with the
word of the Vizier who works for Lord.

117
00:17:58,354 --> 00:18:00,904
Vizier represents Konya.

118
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:04,010
What about you Malhun Hatun?

119
00:18:04,384 --> 00:18:06,444
We'll talk on the behalf of Osman Bey...

120
00:18:07,035 --> 00:18:10,095
...don't think that every word
we utter is only our judgment...

121
00:18:10,558 --> 00:18:12,398
...they're the command of Osman Bey.

122
00:18:15,159 --> 00:18:18,369
Osman Bey only cares for the good of Kayı.

123
00:18:18,658 --> 00:18:20,558
We can all attest to that.

124
00:18:21,248 --> 00:18:22,958
Where is Osman Bey?

125
00:18:23,841 --> 00:18:28,401
In his absence it is appropriate
for his brother to sit on the throne.

126
00:18:28,753 --> 00:18:34,063
Right now, a vacant throne is
better than Gündüz Bey.

127
00:18:34,966 --> 00:18:39,126
Whatever Gündüz Bey does,
he does it for Vizier Alemshah.

128
00:18:40,430 --> 00:18:42,446
Not for the good of the tribe.

129
00:18:42,446 --> 00:18:45,376
You are talking about the son of
Ertuğrul Ghazi here, Demirci!

130
00:18:46,430 --> 00:18:48,978
Gündüz Bey does not act against the tribe!

131
00:18:48,978 --> 00:18:51,178
You are not the one to decide this!

132
00:18:51,836 --> 00:18:54,116
Watch your tone!

133
00:18:54,185 --> 00:18:55,715
I don't get it!

134
00:18:58,938 --> 00:19:00,428
I don't get it.

135
00:19:02,529 --> 00:19:05,999
One sides with justice...

136
00:19:07,072 --> 00:19:09,512
...one sides with Türkmen...

137
00:19:10,192 --> 00:19:12,772
...one sides with the oppressed...

138
00:19:18,809 --> 00:19:21,159
...but how come one does not
side with Osman Bey?

139
00:19:22,598 --> 00:19:24,508
I don't get it.

140
00:19:25,210 --> 00:19:28,170
There is a lot to not
understand, shepherd.

141
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,896
You'll understand eventually.

142
00:19:33,151 --> 00:19:35,681
But everyone will side with Osman Bey,...

143
00:19:36,598 --> 00:19:39,008
...before you know it.

144
00:19:39,861 --> 00:19:42,621
You're all united in lampooning!

145
00:19:43,079 --> 00:19:45,729
You invited us here to get our opinion...

146
00:19:45,838 --> 00:19:47,488
...but interrogating us instead!

147
00:19:47,658 --> 00:19:49,138
Make way!

148
00:20:06,014 --> 00:20:09,214
There is nobody here to
interrogate you Yılmaz Bey.

149
00:20:10,214 --> 00:20:13,604
We trust Osman Bey.

150
00:20:15,263 --> 00:20:16,633
It is our wish that...

151
00:20:17,331 --> 00:20:21,831
...anyone who has doubt
stays away from us.

152
00:20:24,436 --> 00:20:28,556
If you have doubt,
stay away from us,...

153
00:20:28,766 --> 00:20:30,366
...Yımaz Bey.

154
00:20:33,996 --> 00:20:36,686
Harmankaya Castle

155
00:20:36,801 --> 00:20:40,601
If I sit on the throne,
hatuns will not be happy.

156
00:20:41,261 --> 00:20:42,651
It's apparent.

157
00:20:43,664 --> 00:20:46,174
There will be duality,
Vizier Alemshah.

158
00:20:46,575 --> 00:20:50,645
Türkmen likes beys that are
puissant, Gündüz Bey.

159
00:20:52,509 --> 00:20:55,799
I will give you a power so great...

160
00:20:56,746 --> 00:20:59,536
...they will hesitate to object.

161
00:21:00,041 --> 00:21:01,521
Alright,...

162
00:21:02,432 --> 00:21:06,292
...alright, but what is this power
that you are talking about?

163
00:21:08,238 --> 00:21:10,178
Look at these walls.

164
00:21:10,236 --> 00:21:13,216
They're not suitable for the İnegöl flag.

165
00:21:20,594 --> 00:21:22,603
We say that conquest is...

166
00:21:22,603 --> 00:21:25,183
...the salvation of Türkmen.

167
00:21:26,306 --> 00:21:28,876
Should we leave here for the infidels?

168
00:21:34,027 --> 00:21:38,967
From now on, the ornaments of these walls
will be the flag of the illustrious Kayı.

169
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:45,850
Why do you think we came to the
Harmankaya Castle, Gündüz Bey?

170
00:21:55,090 --> 00:21:57,880
I was wondering that too,
Vizier Alemshah.

171
00:22:02,733 --> 00:22:04,943
I wasn't expecting to see you here.

172
00:22:05,554 --> 00:22:06,754
Gündüz Bey?

173
00:22:10,774 --> 00:22:13,144
You look tired, Nikola.

174
00:22:13,523 --> 00:22:16,993
Well, I'm not only the Lord
of İnegöl anymore.

175
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:22,428
I also own the Harmankaya Castle
that you sit on the throne of.

176
00:22:23,363 --> 00:22:24,933
Isn't that right?

177
00:22:26,775 --> 00:22:31,435
And this is worth it for all the
exhaustion, Vizier Alam Shah.

178
00:22:32,701 --> 00:22:34,931
You have earned this Nikola.

179
00:22:35,315 --> 00:22:37,965
By siding with the right side,
you have earned this.

180
00:22:44,343 --> 00:22:47,743
It is not like I'm not going to sit
on this throne forever, Nikola.

181
00:22:48,657 --> 00:22:50,287
It is yours.

182
00:22:54,397 --> 00:22:57,627
Now, tell me about Kosses.

183
00:22:57,875 --> 00:22:59,725
What is his circumstance?

184
00:22:59,832 --> 00:23:02,182
Has he reached emperorship?

185
00:23:16,217 --> 00:23:17,317
Kosses...

186
00:23:19,556 --> 00:23:23,296
...is in a cage as it would fit a traitor.

187
00:23:23,644 --> 00:23:26,064
He is probably going to Constantinople.

188
00:23:28,483 --> 00:23:33,023
When he arrives there, he will prepare
a beautiful ending for the emperor.

189
00:23:42,186 --> 00:23:44,376
I'm thankful to you Alps.

190
00:23:44,664 --> 00:23:47,644
I hope God gives me a long life...

191
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:49,553
...for me to be able to repay you.

192
00:23:50,231 --> 00:23:52,961
We just fulfilled our Bey's command.

193
00:23:53,155 --> 00:23:55,355
If our Bey commands
something, we act upon it.

194
00:23:55,609 --> 00:23:58,009
Now we will go to Konya, Alps.

195
00:23:58,338 --> 00:24:00,498
I know it's a tough road...

196
00:24:00,832 --> 00:24:02,872
...but we'll find a way around it.

197
00:24:03,128 --> 00:24:07,278
And then, with Allah's permission, we will
save Osman Bey before he's taken to Konya.

198
00:24:07,448 --> 00:24:09,968
- If Allah permits my bey.
- If Allah permits my bey.

199
00:24:10,067 --> 00:24:11,723
As I said Kosses,...

200
00:24:11,723 --> 00:24:15,403
...one of the reasons we got you out
of there was to save Osman Bey.

201
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:17,190
I understand.

202
00:24:17,221 --> 00:24:21,141
But for that, I need to send word to my
special unit waiting for me in Harmankaya.

203
00:24:21,141 --> 00:24:25,057
When they join us, it'll be easier
for us to save Osman Bey.

204
00:24:29,070 --> 00:24:32,205
Let them give this ring
to their leader Kiros.

205
00:24:32,205 --> 00:24:34,745
Only then, they'll be convinced it's me.

206
00:24:38,730 --> 00:24:40,450
You know what to do Kutan.

207
00:24:40,630 --> 00:24:42,390
Go to Harmankaya...

208
00:24:42,537 --> 00:24:45,877
...take Kossess' men and follow
us on the way to Konya.

209
00:24:46,336 --> 00:24:48,426
Yes, my bey!

210
00:24:49,386 --> 00:24:52,406
Come on, Alps! We don't
have time! Let's go!

211
00:25:05,764 --> 00:25:10,364
You stay all the way there because
we told you to stay away, Yılmaz Bey?

212
00:25:19,395 --> 00:25:22,365
You misunderstood our Sheik, Yılmaz Bey.

213
00:25:31,612 --> 00:25:36,022
Our wish is for you to do as you say...

214
00:25:36,512 --> 00:25:38,702
...and attain your desires.

215
00:25:40,698 --> 00:25:43,098
May the Lord release your heart...

216
00:25:43,652 --> 00:25:47,672
...from doubt on the path for truth!

217
00:25:49,250 --> 00:25:50,800
May Allah bless you!

218
00:25:54,765 --> 00:25:56,755
We know Kayı's beys for being...

219
00:25:57,570 --> 00:26:01,810
...the ones who dream of holy war,
the ones who are beware of danger...

220
00:26:02,759 --> 00:26:04,589
...and for their love of conquest.

221
00:26:07,468 --> 00:26:11,948
As you should know those holy
wars, those conquests...

222
00:26:12,695 --> 00:26:14,718
...are possible because of Osman Bey.

223
00:26:14,718 --> 00:26:17,068
May Allah bless you!

224
00:26:26,019 --> 00:26:29,729
Your hearts and your fists are strong.

225
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:34,177
Your wish is pure.

226
00:26:34,856 --> 00:26:38,316
On the path for the good of this soil...

227
00:26:38,708 --> 00:26:41,198
...may Allah's truth be with you!

228
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:43,530
- Amen!
- Amen!

229
00:26:44,768 --> 00:26:46,518
- Amen!
- Amen!

230
00:26:46,678 --> 00:26:48,688
May Allah help you hatuns!

231
00:27:06,111 --> 00:27:08,851
I should inform the Vizier.

232
00:27:41,561 --> 00:27:45,331
Osman is being taken to be crushed.

233
00:27:55,970 --> 00:27:57,510
Osman.

234
00:27:58,552 --> 00:28:03,932
I promise that your blood
will shed below ground...

235
00:28:05,335 --> 00:28:09,955
Will be acquainted with Erlik Khan.

236
00:28:35,982 --> 00:28:37,212
My bey,

237
00:28:49,008 --> 00:28:50,378
Forever.

238
00:29:28,464 --> 00:29:33,534
When Geyhatu arrives you will be
crushed under these furious horses...

239
00:29:40,994 --> 00:29:43,334
Their shoes will go through your blood.

240
00:29:43,554 --> 00:29:47,204
Your stench of carrion will be all over.

241
00:29:52,459 --> 00:29:54,899
The horse is the wing of the Turk.

242
00:29:55,826 --> 00:29:58,086
The horse is the will of the Turk.

243
00:29:58,719 --> 00:30:01,719
When did we ever hang back from a horse?

244
00:30:03,115 --> 00:30:04,955
Send the horses!

245
00:30:05,198 --> 00:30:08,610
Even the most furious one
will be calm before us!

246
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:10,196
Come on!

247
00:30:10,196 --> 00:30:13,676
Geyhatu will finish the
ritual and join us.

248
00:30:14,786 --> 00:30:18,756
When that time comes, all
of you will die suffering!

249
00:30:19,314 --> 00:30:22,104
The most painful way possible.

250
00:30:50,252 --> 00:30:53,492
The end of the traitors is painful.

251
00:30:55,561 --> 00:30:58,121
The end of the traitors
like you is obvious.

252
00:31:12,118 --> 00:31:15,528
We'll unite and arise from the dead!

253
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:18,929
But your end will be much worse!

254
00:31:22,350 --> 00:31:24,200
Brother, hang on!

255
00:31:24,596 --> 00:31:26,586
Your reckoning will be worse!

256
00:31:29,735 --> 00:31:32,055
Leave him alone you filth!

257
00:31:32,164 --> 00:31:33,974
Leave him alone you dog!

258
00:31:37,713 --> 00:31:40,023
Hang on, Cerkutay!
Hang on!

259
00:31:48,752 --> 00:31:50,852
Geyhatun is coming sir.

260
00:31:53,406 --> 00:31:55,436
Get the horses ready!

261
00:31:56,413 --> 00:31:59,463
We will start when Geyhatu comes.

262
00:32:10,874 --> 00:32:13,654
Brother, are you well?

263
00:32:13,957 --> 00:32:15,527
My bey,...

264
00:32:30,486 --> 00:32:32,616
May I come in my Vizier?

265
00:32:32,748 --> 00:32:34,048
You may come in.

266
00:32:40,563 --> 00:32:41,833
My Vizier,...

267
00:32:44,223 --> 00:32:46,983
...Osman Bey's Hatuns are
assembled at the monastery.

268
00:32:48,182 --> 00:32:50,132
They invited the beys as well.

269
00:32:50,252 --> 00:32:52,232
They are up to someting.

270
00:32:56,284 --> 00:32:59,464
It looks like the hatuns won't
behave themselves, Gündüz Bey.

271
00:33:01,650 --> 00:33:03,950
They'll make a big deal of you...

272
00:33:04,759 --> 00:33:08,299
...sitting on the throne to their beys.

273
00:33:08,882 --> 00:33:14,142
As long as they're in the tribe, we
won't be able to prevent duality.

274
00:33:15,481 --> 00:33:18,391
For that, the best thing we can do is...

275
00:33:19,744 --> 00:33:21,984
...to banish them.

276
00:33:25,158 --> 00:33:27,448
That includes Selcan Hatun.

277
00:33:29,178 --> 00:33:32,528
What are you saying Vizier Alam Shah?

278
00:33:34,158 --> 00:33:39,028
I've done everything I have for my tribe.

279
00:33:40,383 --> 00:33:42,923
Even if one person has trouble...

280
00:33:44,166 --> 00:33:46,366
...that throne is haram for me.

281
00:33:47,432 --> 00:33:50,882
Now, if I banish my mother,
my brother's hatuns...

282
00:33:51,077 --> 00:33:53,877
...my sisters...

283
00:33:55,736 --> 00:33:57,746
...where is unity then?

284
00:33:58,130 --> 00:34:01,195
Günzüd Bey, that's the right thing to do.

285
00:34:01,195 --> 00:34:03,985
There is nothing righteous
about this Vizier Alam Shah.

286
00:34:05,743 --> 00:34:07,703
Where there is oppression...

287
00:34:07,749 --> 00:34:09,859
...there is no morals.

288
00:34:10,164 --> 00:34:14,583
Now, If I banish the
hatuns of my tribe...

289
00:34:16,626 --> 00:34:18,846
...how could I sit on that throne?

290
00:34:19,130 --> 00:34:21,860
How could I be known as a Bey in my tribe?

291
00:34:26,538 --> 00:34:28,338
Do you know why...

292
00:34:28,853 --> 00:34:33,112
...that throne belongs to you, Gündüz Bey?

293
00:34:35,339 --> 00:34:37,259
This is it.

294
00:34:38,188 --> 00:34:40,118
Your compassion.

295
00:34:40,684 --> 00:34:45,364
I know that your compassion will
always overcome your greed.

296
00:34:47,373 --> 00:34:49,993
My wish is not to sit on the throne.

297
00:34:50,918 --> 00:34:53,299
But to be a friend to your community.

298
00:34:54,952 --> 00:34:57,152
But know that...

299
00:34:57,848 --> 00:35:00,428
...to be a friend to your community...

300
00:35:00,898 --> 00:35:03,498
...we should fight off the sedition.

301
00:35:05,527 --> 00:35:07,947
Who is responsible for the sedition?

302
00:35:10,573 --> 00:35:12,433
Hatuns.

303
00:35:12,983 --> 00:35:14,973
That's not how it works.

304
00:35:16,403 --> 00:35:21,643
I've never said any of the things you've
said as you can assume, Vizier Alam Shah.

305
00:35:25,445 --> 00:35:27,395
Godspeed!

306
00:35:53,350 --> 00:35:54,960
May Allah bless you Kutan!

307
00:35:55,029 --> 00:35:56,869
May Allah bless you, my bey!

308
00:36:06,881 --> 00:36:09,121
My noble warriors!

309
00:36:15,628 --> 00:36:16,568
Kiros.

310
00:36:22,349 --> 00:36:25,209
I'm always loyal to you Lord Kosses.

311
00:36:26,344 --> 00:36:28,164
So are my soldiers.

312
00:36:31,506 --> 00:36:33,626
Our loyalty will end only when we're dead.

313
00:36:35,180 --> 00:36:37,340
- I know.
- We're with you, sir.

314
00:36:39,069 --> 00:36:43,439
To save Osman Bey, we will
help Turgut Bey and his alps.

315
00:36:47,207 --> 00:36:48,917
My alps are on their way to Konya.

316
00:36:49,528 --> 00:36:51,618
We will find Osman Bey.

317
00:36:53,421 --> 00:36:55,421
As you wish.

318
00:36:57,758 --> 00:37:01,048
We will not spare the horses...

319
00:37:01,711 --> 00:37:04,521
...until we get Osman Bey!

320
00:37:05,965 --> 00:37:08,595
Whatever needs to be done,
will be done Turgut Bey.

321
00:37:10,861 --> 00:37:12,401
Come on!

322
00:37:12,897 --> 00:37:14,127
Let's go.

323
00:37:14,852 --> 00:37:16,792
Come on, soldiers!

324
00:37:22,588 --> 00:37:23,968
Come on!

325
00:37:37,836 --> 00:37:40,776
The steel of these weapons
came from Halep.

326
00:37:41,014 --> 00:37:43,914
These are the sharpest
weapons of this soil.

327
00:37:53,710 --> 00:37:56,150
Is something going on behind
my back at the tribe?

328
00:37:56,803 --> 00:37:59,103
Who are these people you
are giving weapons to?

329
00:37:59,763 --> 00:38:02,513
They're the new alps of
Osman Bey, Gündüz Bey.

330
00:38:09,243 --> 00:38:12,213
Do you hear what you're
saying, blacksmith?

331
00:38:14,211 --> 00:38:16,121
Don't play word games and tell me!

332
00:38:16,175 --> 00:38:17,595
Who are these alps?

333
00:38:17,696 --> 00:38:20,806
When have I ever played word
games, Gündüz Bey?

334
00:38:21,562 --> 00:38:25,222
As I said, they're the new
alps of Osman Bey.

335
00:38:25,571 --> 00:38:29,311
You get alps for the tribe
without my permission?

336
00:38:31,909 --> 00:38:33,569
I ask for the last time...

337
00:38:33,945 --> 00:38:35,815
...who are these alps...

338
00:38:35,959 --> 00:38:37,719
...and where do they come from?

339
00:38:38,028 --> 00:38:40,328
From the Kızılbey Oğlu tribe.

340
00:38:47,637 --> 00:38:49,657
They come from the soil of our ancestors.

341
00:38:51,342 --> 00:38:54,742
The ones who try to do things
we do not want are the...

342
00:38:54,918 --> 00:38:57,108
...valiants who will stand by us.

343
00:38:59,364 --> 00:39:02,454
I am the one to decide what
ought to be done or not.

344
00:39:04,295 --> 00:39:06,725
But, it s not time for it.

345
00:39:07,989 --> 00:39:10,269
I waiting for all of you at the tent.

346
00:39:12,503 --> 00:39:14,233
You too blacksmith.

347
00:39:38,757 --> 00:39:40,507
Alps!

348
00:39:40,507 --> 00:39:42,167
Let's go!

349
00:39:47,885 --> 00:39:50,025
Praise be!

350
00:39:58,998 --> 00:40:00,518
Ride!

351
00:40:58,313 --> 00:40:59,793
Kosses!

352
00:41:03,022 --> 00:41:04,752
Praise be!

353
00:41:04,757 --> 00:41:06,907
How do you say it Osman Bey?

354
00:41:06,930 --> 00:41:08,960
May Allah bless you!

355
00:41:23,597 --> 00:41:25,077
Osman Bey!

356
00:41:30,152 --> 00:41:31,882
Kosses!

357
00:41:35,554 --> 00:41:37,324
I'm here valiants!

358
00:41:44,732 --> 00:41:47,412
Thank you, Allah!

359
00:41:48,502 --> 00:41:49,986
Are you well?

360
00:41:49,986 --> 00:41:53,546
This is not just revenge,
it's more than that.

361
00:41:53,649 --> 00:41:55,281
This is war!

362
00:41:55,281 --> 00:41:58,621
Forgive me, Osman Bey I haven't
gotten my revenge yet...

363
00:41:58,712 --> 00:42:01,142
...also, the husband of my sister is...

364
00:42:01,977 --> 00:42:04,107
...very insistent.

365
00:42:07,042 --> 00:42:08,752
Osman Bey!

366
00:42:09,876 --> 00:42:12,146
Osman Bey, blood shall
not spill on the ground.

367
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:15,070
But we need to go, more will come!

368
00:42:19,033 --> 00:42:20,643
Alps!

369
00:42:22,553 --> 00:42:24,533
We're withdrawing!

370
00:42:25,691 --> 00:42:27,481
Come on!

371
00:42:27,714 --> 00:42:29,084
Come on!

372
00:42:31,403 --> 00:42:34,013
Kiros, we're withdrawing!

373
00:42:42,924 --> 00:42:44,914
Let's go!

374
00:42:49,746 --> 00:42:51,196
Malhun Hatun,...

375
00:42:53,104 --> 00:42:55,384
...those alps won't stay in this tribe.

376
00:42:56,566 --> 00:42:58,716
They'll go where they came from.

377
00:42:59,966 --> 00:43:02,076
Alps will stay here, Gündüz Bey.

378
00:43:03,878 --> 00:43:07,688
They'll stay so that you can stop
dreaming about being a Bey.

379
00:43:08,970 --> 00:43:13,060
Alps will stay here until
Osman Bey returns.

380
00:43:13,489 --> 00:43:15,379
That is the command of my bey.

381
00:43:16,596 --> 00:43:19,796
It is apparent that, that Vizier
tricked you with his snake tongue.

382
00:43:20,557 --> 00:43:22,687
But we will wake you up.

383
00:43:22,963 --> 00:43:25,243
We will not let you set up that feast!

384
00:43:31,038 --> 00:43:33,968
You won't let me set up the feast huh?

385
00:43:38,014 --> 00:43:39,604
Good.

386
00:43:40,541 --> 00:43:42,051
Good, then.

387
00:43:43,423 --> 00:43:45,223
Gather your things...

388
00:43:47,414 --> 00:43:49,674
...you cannot stay at this
tribe any longer.

389
00:43:51,076 --> 00:43:52,266
What?

390
00:43:55,467 --> 00:43:57,277
I'll banish you!

391
00:43:59,176 --> 00:44:02,606
Kayı Tribe will not exist without a bey!

392
00:44:09,136 --> 00:44:13,316
The feast will be set up, and me
the only suitable bey...

393
00:44:17,120 --> 00:44:18,640
...me...

394
00:44:18,881 --> 00:44:21,551
...the son of Ertuğrul Ghazi,
Gündüz Bey...

395
00:44:24,690 --> 00:44:27,530
...will be the bey of Kayı
Tribe, chosen with a feast.

396
00:45:17,304 --> 00:45:19,624
Where is Osman?

397
00:45:25,443 --> 00:45:27,253
Where is Osman?

398
00:45:34,039 --> 00:45:35,589
Osman...

399
00:45:36,851 --> 00:45:41,821
...I will rip your heart off
with my bare hands!

400
00:45:49,349 --> 00:45:52,999
For the sake of not having
duality in the tribe...

401
00:45:53,525 --> 00:45:56,385
...you will be banished to the
frontier village in İnegöl.

402
00:45:56,457 --> 00:45:58,467
What are you saying Gündüz Bey?

403
00:45:58,560 --> 00:46:00,369
Whose feast is this?

404
00:46:00,369 --> 00:46:05,219
It is the feast of the one who puts the
good of the tribe above all else, mother!

405
00:46:08,170 --> 00:46:10,020
Don't go against me!

406
00:46:15,466 --> 00:46:18,186
I won't let you do this, Gündüz Bey!

407
00:46:20,858 --> 00:46:23,528
Forget whatever it is that you're thinking

408
00:46:29,335 --> 00:46:33,865
Whoever does not respect the
command of a Bey and creates duality...

409
00:46:34,588 --> 00:46:38,488
...will be banished from the tribe
without hesitation!

410
00:46:43,231 --> 00:46:44,971
I won't hesitate!

411
00:46:46,535 --> 00:46:48,835
You are the one creating
duality, Gündüz Bey!

412
00:46:50,470 --> 00:46:52,654
Looks like the taste of
the throne was sweet.

413
00:46:52,654 --> 00:46:54,844
You're terrified of not sitting on it.

414
00:46:56,142 --> 00:47:00,392
Even the thought of Osman Bey recuperating
terrifies you, right, Gündüz Bey?

415
00:47:01,595 --> 00:47:05,409
If you're so afraid of us
you're probably up to...

416
00:47:05,409 --> 00:47:07,868
...something so that Osman Bey
does not come back.

417
00:47:07,868 --> 00:47:10,378
I cannot set my tribe on fire to...

418
00:47:10,526 --> 00:47:13,596
...appeal to you Bala Hatun.

419
00:47:16,591 --> 00:47:18,951
You do not want to understand me.

420
00:47:20,150 --> 00:47:21,900
I can see that.

421
00:47:22,758 --> 00:47:27,088
For the good of all of us, until
there is order in the tribe...

422
00:47:28,066 --> 00:47:29,966
...you will stay in the village!

423
00:47:40,317 --> 00:47:44,667
Even his uncle betrayed
Osman Bey like this.

424
00:47:46,317 --> 00:47:48,367
How can you degrade yourself to this?

425
00:47:49,620 --> 00:47:52,810
Let's say you left your mind in
the palm of that Vizier's hand...

426
00:47:53,704 --> 00:47:55,224
...what about your heart?

427
00:47:55,598 --> 00:47:58,148
Your heart is in the palm
of his hand as well?

428
00:47:58,265 --> 00:48:00,325
What kind of cruelty is this?

429
00:48:03,444 --> 00:48:05,514
Mother, you have a rough tongue.

430
00:48:05,998 --> 00:48:07,848
Do I?

431
00:48:08,389 --> 00:48:10,389
Do I?

432
00:48:11,541 --> 00:48:14,431
You pray that your aunt
has a rough tongue.

433
00:48:15,368 --> 00:48:17,708
If it was your deceased mother...

434
00:48:18,343 --> 00:48:20,253
...she would spit in your face.

435
00:48:22,031 --> 00:48:26,281
In your veins, you have the blood of your
ancestor Süleyman Shah, Ertuğrul Ghazi!

436
00:48:26,577 --> 00:48:28,547
Aren't you ashamed?

437
00:48:30,480 --> 00:48:32,530
Who am I speaking to?

438
00:48:34,548 --> 00:48:38,498
This person in front of
me is not my Gündüz.

439
00:48:41,039 --> 00:48:44,299
There is no blood nor love in his face.

440
00:48:46,661 --> 00:48:48,821
Know this, Gündüz Bey,...

441
00:48:49,646 --> 00:48:52,576
...that from now on, for me...

442
00:48:52,795 --> 00:48:57,575
...you are an unlovely, bloodless
lowlife just like that Vizier!

443
00:49:02,633 --> 00:49:05,203
What kind of remarks are these?

444
00:49:08,077 --> 00:49:10,837
It seems I made the right thing...

445
00:49:11,698 --> 00:49:13,948
...banishing you.

446
00:49:14,004 --> 00:49:15,124
Enough!

447
00:49:25,124 --> 00:49:27,494
You will leave this tribe tomorrow!

448
00:49:31,462 --> 00:49:33,822
You will stay there until...

449
00:49:38,089 --> 00:49:40,009
...you decide to unite.

450
00:49:47,509 --> 00:49:48,859
I'm well.

451
00:50:00,372 --> 00:50:02,402
Vizier and Nikola...

452
00:50:02,465 --> 00:50:04,485
...they took the pen from me.

453
00:50:04,852 --> 00:50:08,862
Nikola's flag is waving in the walls
of Harmakaya Castle, right now.

454
00:50:10,456 --> 00:50:14,576
The castle, they gave Harmankaya
to Nikola, you say?

455
00:50:15,126 --> 00:50:16,616
Yes.

456
00:50:19,828 --> 00:50:22,408
There is nothing for the Lords in the...

457
00:50:22,806 --> 00:50:25,686
...order Vizier says he will bring Kosses.

458
00:50:26,273 --> 00:50:28,423
He is only out for his own power.

459
00:50:29,810 --> 00:50:33,980
His only desire is to subsume the
Turkmen people under him.

460
00:50:35,419 --> 00:50:37,179
Vizier Alam Shah.

461
00:50:40,441 --> 00:50:41,741
Before the feast...

462
00:50:43,198 --> 00:50:45,568
...he will give Harmankaya to my brother.

463
00:50:47,079 --> 00:50:52,059
He'll give it to him so that Gündüz
Bey can become the Bey of Kayı.

464
00:50:54,266 --> 00:50:57,066
The power of Kayı is the most
important thing for him.

465
00:50:59,449 --> 00:51:01,589
How can you be so sure of it Osman Bey?

466
00:51:02,512 --> 00:51:05,902
Infidels are good at
playing games, Kosses.

467
00:51:07,218 --> 00:51:11,228
I am good at spoiling those games.

468
00:51:16,830 --> 00:51:20,930
Now, take your most trusted man.

469
00:51:22,199 --> 00:51:24,459
Let him inform Nikola about the game.

470
00:51:24,749 --> 00:51:26,459
How Osman Bey?

471
00:51:26,701 --> 00:51:29,631
We're going to work on
the behalf of Nikola now?

472
00:51:31,412 --> 00:51:33,872
No, there is time for everything.

473
00:51:35,570 --> 00:51:37,490
Right now, what we will do is...

474
00:51:38,569 --> 00:51:43,939
...stopping my brother that will sit on
Kayı's throne with Vizier's doing.

475
00:51:46,367 --> 00:51:48,617
He deserves this.

476
00:51:49,087 --> 00:51:50,377
I get you.

477
00:51:50,763 --> 00:51:52,533
Kiros,...

478
00:51:52,924 --> 00:51:54,924
...go to Nikola immediately.

479
00:51:55,008 --> 00:51:58,188
Spell out what Osman Bey has said.

480
00:51:58,188 --> 00:51:59,598
Quickly.

481
00:52:04,631 --> 00:52:07,351
- Turgut Bey,
- Yes, Osman Bey.

482
00:52:07,561 --> 00:52:10,021
Inform a couple of alps

483
00:52:10,987 --> 00:52:14,447
Let them bury my brother Göktuğ and...

484
00:52:15,007 --> 00:52:17,667
...other martyrs as it
would fit the heroes.

485
00:52:17,829 --> 00:52:20,129
We're heading towards the edge...

486
00:52:20,486 --> 00:52:22,226
...we'll do it, Osman Bey.

487
00:52:27,390 --> 00:52:29,150
We'll ride our horses inside...

488
00:52:30,798 --> 00:52:33,018
...not towards the edge!

489
00:52:40,313 --> 00:52:41,673
Kutan!

490
00:52:43,502 --> 00:52:46,102
Send five alps to the place
where our brothers died.

491
00:52:46,849 --> 00:52:48,479
Yes, my bey.

492
00:52:51,026 --> 00:52:54,946
I don't get it. Did we endanger
our lives for nothing, Osman Bey?

493
00:52:55,792 --> 00:52:57,452
After all that has happened...

494
00:52:57,704 --> 00:53:01,434
...you will go to Seljuk that could not
even protect you when you were captive?

495
00:53:02,660 --> 00:53:04,040
Sultan Mesut...

496
00:53:05,386 --> 00:53:07,866
...is the Sultan of Seljuk.

497
00:53:09,639 --> 00:53:11,839
I'm his bey.

498
00:53:15,115 --> 00:53:17,135
I need to go to Konya.

499
00:53:17,235 --> 00:53:19,655
It's only you, Osman Bey.

500
00:53:20,633 --> 00:53:22,703
What if you never come back?

501
00:53:24,427 --> 00:53:25,977
What if they hurt you?

502
00:53:25,977 --> 00:53:27,487
What will we do then?

503
00:53:27,487 --> 00:53:29,437
They'll hurt me easier there.

504
00:53:31,631 --> 00:53:35,101
They tried their luck at Bilecik.

505
00:53:36,166 --> 00:53:37,626
For what?

506
00:53:39,864 --> 00:53:42,084
Geyhatu and Alam Shah...

507
00:53:43,440 --> 00:53:45,480
...it seems that they're
working together.

508
00:53:47,460 --> 00:53:50,590
They don't want me to go to Sultan.

509
00:53:51,464 --> 00:53:53,424
That is why...

510
00:53:54,186 --> 00:53:58,046
...I will tell Sultan everything.

511
00:53:59,869 --> 00:54:01,839
He'll know what's what.

512
00:54:02,161 --> 00:54:04,231
He'll agree with me.

513
00:54:04,671 --> 00:54:08,351
If so, I won't leave you alone.

514
00:54:08,849 --> 00:54:10,171
I will join you.

515
00:54:10,171 --> 00:54:13,181
Also, I know just the person
who will let us in the palace.

516
00:54:17,959 --> 00:54:20,849
You did not leave me when I needed,...

517
00:54:22,888 --> 00:54:24,758
...If so,...

518
00:54:25,820 --> 00:54:27,680
...I'm coming with you, Osman Bey.

519
00:54:28,586 --> 00:54:31,016
Let's ride our horses to
Konya immediately.

520
00:54:34,744 --> 00:54:36,914
Praise be!

521
00:54:42,039 --> 00:54:43,409
Let's go!

522
00:54:43,689 --> 00:54:45,339
Mount up, then!

523
00:54:46,479 --> 00:54:47,419
Let's go!

524
00:54:47,519 --> 00:54:49,839
Come on, horses!

525
00:55:08,509 --> 00:55:10,719
Sir, Turks have changed their route.

526
00:55:11,194 --> 00:55:13,024
What does that mean?

527
00:55:13,223 --> 00:55:15,223
Sir, they're heading to Konya.

528
00:55:22,968 --> 00:55:24,718
Osman...

529
00:55:25,339 --> 00:55:29,589
...will solve what he couldn't with
a weapon, with a word.

530
00:55:30,313 --> 00:55:32,443
He is heading to Sultan.

531
00:55:37,407 --> 00:55:41,827
I can take the fastest horse to catch up
to him and cut his head off.

532
00:55:43,104 --> 00:55:44,764
No need.

533
00:55:46,484 --> 00:55:50,434
Let him go to Sultan.

534
00:55:53,398 --> 00:55:54,898
Osman...

535
00:55:55,279 --> 00:55:57,799
...has no idea.

536
00:55:59,761 --> 00:56:04,201
He's riding his horse towards his demise.

537
00:56:15,941 --> 00:56:18,421
We should inform the people immediately.

538
00:56:18,727 --> 00:56:20,597
You are right, Bala Hatun.

539
00:56:20,940 --> 00:56:23,270
Most of the beys are with us.

540
00:56:23,315 --> 00:56:25,638
If Allah permits they'll still be with us.

541
00:56:25,758 --> 00:56:27,068
If Allah permits!

542
00:56:30,247 --> 00:56:32,957
The horses that belong to Osman
Bey are with us as well.

543
00:56:33,091 --> 00:56:37,581
If they can't be diplomatic, then we will
draw our weapons out of our holsters!

544
00:56:38,515 --> 00:56:40,485
It's time for action.

545
00:56:40,709 --> 00:56:43,979
We will keep our word and
not give up on our case!

546
00:56:44,496 --> 00:56:47,406
We will protect Osman Bey's trust
whatever it takes!

547
00:56:47,781 --> 00:56:49,531
We will!

548
00:56:49,872 --> 00:56:52,032
May Allah bless you!

549
00:56:52,251 --> 00:56:54,741
Osman Bey's trust is in good hands.

550
00:57:00,482 --> 00:57:03,132
You were correct, Vizier Alam Shah.

551
00:57:03,869 --> 00:57:05,789
You were correct.

552
00:57:07,717 --> 00:57:09,577
Hatuns won't stay back.

553
00:57:10,700 --> 00:57:13,210
They are creating duality at
the tribe already.

554
00:57:16,351 --> 00:57:20,101
On behalf of who are they doing this?

555
00:57:23,727 --> 00:57:25,177
My brother.

556
00:57:26,725 --> 00:57:28,135
Osman.

557
00:57:29,743 --> 00:57:31,783
He wants it so that...

558
00:57:33,228 --> 00:57:35,858
...he won't let me sit on that throne.

559
00:57:36,437 --> 00:57:38,397
As you can see Gündüz Bey,

560
00:57:38,968 --> 00:57:43,008
your brother Osman is messing up
your tribe from Konya.

561
00:57:43,829 --> 00:57:45,669
Creating duality.

562
00:57:45,902 --> 00:57:47,612
A bey cannot act like that!

563
00:57:48,607 --> 00:57:52,157
You need to think of your people.

564
00:57:54,242 --> 00:57:57,822
You will be a good bey, Gündüz Bey.

565
00:57:58,899 --> 00:58:01,769
You'll think of your people
before anything else.

566
00:58:02,956 --> 00:58:07,056
That's why you should banish them.

567
00:58:10,707 --> 00:58:12,787
I've already done that.

568
00:58:14,367 --> 00:58:16,247
Done it and now I'm here.

569
00:58:17,534 --> 00:58:21,714
I made the decision to banish them.

570
00:58:22,870 --> 00:58:26,560
You did the right thing for
your tribe, Gündüz Bey.

571
00:58:28,140 --> 00:58:30,420
Don't be sad over them.

572
00:58:31,618 --> 00:58:33,798
Thank you. But,...

573
00:58:35,209 --> 00:58:39,879
...it doesn't seem like neither my
mother nor hatuns will leave easily.

574
00:58:41,935 --> 00:58:46,055
May Allah help so that this thing resolves
before anyone draws their weapons.

575
00:58:49,862 --> 00:58:52,752
Don't worry about all of this.

576
00:58:53,333 --> 00:58:57,183
I will stop those who disrupt the order.

577
00:59:00,227 --> 00:59:02,767
Hatuns will go by tomorrow.

578
00:59:04,707 --> 00:59:06,877
Don't worry about it.

579
00:59:26,686 --> 00:59:30,026
I saw you with Osman Bey before.

580
00:59:31,397 --> 00:59:33,547
Now you're Gündüz Bey's alp?

581
00:59:34,278 --> 00:59:36,618
It's the command of Osman Bey.

582
00:59:37,952 --> 00:59:42,772
I have to stand with whoever sits
on the throne of Kayı.

583
00:59:45,338 --> 00:59:47,208
So you would stand against your bey...

584
00:59:47,465 --> 00:59:49,285
...for your bey right?

585
00:59:50,776 --> 00:59:53,356
I'm not against him!

586
00:59:54,634 --> 00:59:58,914
When Osman Bey comes I will
be standing beside him again.

587
01:00:04,231 --> 01:00:06,201
When my bey comes.

588
01:00:07,630 --> 01:00:09,740
Is Osman Bey more important than...

589
01:00:10,566 --> 01:00:12,796
...the good of the tribe,...

590
01:00:13,382 --> 01:00:15,402
...the good of the Turks?

591
01:00:16,272 --> 01:00:17,752
Don't you have reason?

592
01:00:17,805 --> 01:00:19,005
You think?

593
01:00:20,731 --> 01:00:22,471
If so, tell me.

594
01:00:23,969 --> 01:00:25,729
Shut up!

595
01:00:28,850 --> 01:00:31,190
Only snakes work with snakes.

596
01:00:33,555 --> 01:00:35,695
You say, Turk,...

597
01:00:36,472 --> 01:00:39,472
...Kayı and poison us.

598
01:00:42,189 --> 01:00:44,329
Your tongue is like a snake's tongue.

599
01:00:45,168 --> 01:00:48,558
No valiant is without a sin.

600
01:00:50,126 --> 01:00:52,806
If I hurt your feeling,
I apologize, Boran Alp.

601
01:00:54,741 --> 01:00:56,951
I'll make it up to you.

602
01:01:01,117 --> 01:01:03,037
You see?

603
01:01:04,337 --> 01:01:06,227
I see.

604
01:01:07,280 --> 01:01:09,210
Now, tell me.

605
01:01:10,078 --> 01:01:11,978
If I hear you need me...

606
01:01:13,250 --> 01:01:15,060
...where can I find you?

607
01:01:17,013 --> 01:01:19,583
If I can find myself...

608
01:01:20,976 --> 01:01:23,146
...you'll find me.

609
01:01:24,674 --> 01:01:27,554
ON THE WAY TO KERVANSARAY

610
01:01:28,900 --> 01:01:31,920
Cevahir is closer to me
than my brother, Osman Bey.

611
01:01:31,950 --> 01:01:33,832
May Allah bless you brother!

612
01:01:33,832 --> 01:01:36,402
- You're the same way for me.
- May Allah bless you!

613
01:01:36,402 --> 01:01:38,078
Cevahir is a soldier at the palace.

614
01:01:38,078 --> 01:01:40,918
He will lead the unit that will
secure the palace tomorrow.

615
01:01:44,226 --> 01:01:46,626
When you arrive at the
presence of Sultan...

616
01:01:46,711 --> 01:01:49,411
...We will enter the palace
with my brother Cevahir.

617
01:01:50,489 --> 01:01:53,219
Entering and exiting the palace
is easy for me.

618
01:01:53,267 --> 01:01:58,347
If we ever need to escape I know
a secret exit.

619
01:02:03,821 --> 01:02:05,551
We'll exit from there.

620
01:02:08,856 --> 01:02:11,776
May Allah bless you, brother!
We cannot repay you, Thank you.

621
01:02:11,776 --> 01:02:13,151
Thank you.

622
01:02:13,838 --> 01:02:16,988
There is no one that doesn't
know about Osman Bey's valiantness.

623
01:02:17,358 --> 01:02:20,818
There is nothing I wouldn't do
for him or for you my brother.

624
01:02:21,464 --> 01:02:23,174
May Allah bless you!

625
01:02:25,689 --> 01:02:27,769
These are for you Osman Bey.

626
01:02:29,770 --> 01:02:33,020
You've been through all kinds of
trouble, thought you may need it.

627
01:02:36,970 --> 01:02:38,838
Thank you, brother Cevahir!

628
01:02:38,850 --> 01:02:40,550
You thought well!

629
01:02:40,689 --> 01:02:42,264
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey.

630
01:02:42,264 --> 01:02:45,722
I will not be comfortable waiting here...

631
01:02:45,722 --> 01:02:48,272
...while you're out there
in danger Osman Bey.

632
01:02:48,569 --> 01:02:50,319
I would like to join you.

633
01:02:51,441 --> 01:02:54,011
We do not know what's going to
happen inside, Kosses.

634
01:02:55,095 --> 01:02:58,825
If anything goes down, we'll
need you and the alps.

635
01:03:00,478 --> 01:03:04,058
Stay near the palace with the alps.

636
01:03:05,485 --> 01:03:08,815
Of course, I hope everything
goes as we wish...

637
01:03:09,565 --> 01:03:11,435
...but if anything happens...

638
01:03:11,435 --> 01:03:13,305
...you do not need to worry.

639
01:03:13,842 --> 01:03:15,482
May Allah bless you, Kosses!

640
01:03:16,991 --> 01:03:18,901
I will solve this!

641
01:03:19,489 --> 01:03:24,429
I will shine the darkness of lies and
greed with the light of the truth.

642
01:03:26,357 --> 01:03:29,027
Sultan Mesut will know of the truth.

643
01:03:36,934 --> 01:03:39,784
Tomorrow, we will send
men to Kayı Tribe, Konur.

644
01:03:41,009 --> 01:03:42,809
Be ready!

645
01:03:44,096 --> 01:03:46,586
Will we attack the tribe, sir?

646
01:03:51,406 --> 01:03:54,196
If we have to Konur.

647
01:03:55,957 --> 01:03:58,177
My wish is that we won't have to.

648
01:03:59,660 --> 01:04:01,800
Our hope is not to shed blood.

649
01:04:03,085 --> 01:04:06,185
We will have our soldiers
surround them so that...

650
01:04:06,928 --> 01:04:09,908
...they can be afraid and stand back.

651
01:04:12,267 --> 01:04:15,157
If they don't stand back...

652
01:04:15,500 --> 01:04:20,220
...know that the blood of rebels
is halal for us, Konur.

653
01:04:24,317 --> 01:04:28,947
Some rebel hatuns blood is not
more important than the tribe.

654
01:04:31,005 --> 01:04:33,155
We will do what we have to.

655
01:04:33,505 --> 01:04:35,885
Get the soldiers ready as soon as you can.

656
01:04:37,239 --> 01:04:39,269
Yes, Vizier your excellency.

657
01:04:51,106 --> 01:04:55,376
Geyhatu probably has Osman's head by now.

658
01:04:57,779 --> 01:05:02,569
I will go to see him with Kayı
in the palm of my hand.

659
01:05:06,542 --> 01:05:09,962
No one will be able to stop us.

660
01:05:12,190 --> 01:05:15,290
Inegol Castle

661
01:05:16,320 --> 01:05:18,194
Where is that man?

662
01:05:18,194 --> 01:05:21,036
Where the hell is Kosses?
Where is he?

663
01:05:21,036 --> 01:05:23,406
Maybe Rogatus...

664
01:05:23,915 --> 01:05:26,251
...Rogatus and Kosses may have met.

665
01:05:26,251 --> 01:05:29,381
Everything is possible, Julia!

666
01:05:30,268 --> 01:05:33,638
However, there's one thing I am sure of...

667
01:05:34,711 --> 01:05:40,371
...and that is that Kosses will want to
take Harmankaya back before all.

668
01:05:42,112 --> 01:05:45,662
Because the fact that I rule
Harmankaya, like Inegol...

669
01:05:45,899 --> 01:05:49,079
...makes me superior
to the other Lords.

670
01:05:49,177 --> 01:05:51,387
My enemies are aware of that fact as well!

671
01:05:53,734 --> 01:05:55,344
Julia.

672
01:05:55,572 --> 01:05:57,852
Gather your best soldiers.

673
01:05:57,859 --> 01:06:01,569
Deploy them to protect Harmankaya.

674
01:06:01,724 --> 01:06:04,454
They should be able to observe
everything...

675
01:06:04,495 --> 01:06:07,465
...but no one shall notice them.

676
01:06:08,185 --> 01:06:10,225
Be their head.

677
01:06:10,272 --> 01:06:12,322
Don't worry, Lord Nikola.

678
01:06:12,571 --> 01:06:15,661
Harmankaya Castle will be under
the protection of our soldiers.

679
01:06:15,773 --> 01:06:17,423
Good.

680
01:06:17,525 --> 01:06:18,985
Good.

681
01:06:24,988 --> 01:06:27,108
I will not let anyone take over...

682
01:06:28,300 --> 01:06:31,640
...my supremacy and power.

683
01:06:33,022 --> 01:06:36,182
I will destroy anyone...

684
01:06:36,391 --> 01:06:40,171
...whoever crosses my way.

685
01:06:41,684 --> 01:06:43,334
Anyone.

686
01:06:50,230 --> 01:06:52,080
Argos.

687
01:06:55,245 --> 01:06:56,905
Sir.

688
01:06:57,450 --> 01:07:00,420
Kilos, among the commanders of Harmankaya...

689
01:07:01,274 --> 01:07:03,284
...wants to talk to you.

690
01:07:06,131 --> 01:07:07,881
Lord Nikola.

691
01:07:08,129 --> 01:07:10,679
Vizier Alam Shah is doing business
behind your back.

692
01:07:12,195 --> 01:07:15,025
He'll take the castle from you
and give it to Gunduz Bey.

693
01:07:22,362 --> 01:07:25,262
Why would I believe you, commander?

694
01:07:28,007 --> 01:07:32,397
How can I be sure that you are
not one of Kosses' men?

695
01:07:33,934 --> 01:07:35,614
Right?

696
01:07:38,656 --> 01:07:41,036
Kosses is no longer in Harmankaya.

697
01:07:42,475 --> 01:07:45,315
And I do not want to see Turkish flag
in this castle.

698
01:07:46,531 --> 01:07:49,561
So just that, right?

699
01:07:50,661 --> 01:07:53,491
Yes.
This is all I have.

700
01:07:54,417 --> 01:07:55,977
Lord Nikola.

701
01:07:59,220 --> 01:08:01,070
Get out.

702
01:08:02,775 --> 01:08:04,285
All of you.

703
01:08:09,929 --> 01:08:12,129
Vizier Alam Shah.

704
01:08:15,043 --> 01:08:17,542
Vizier Alam Shah.

705
01:08:20,661 --> 01:08:22,861
Vizier Alam Shah.

706
01:08:24,997 --> 01:08:26,877
Vizier Alam Shah!

707
01:08:29,133 --> 01:08:31,863
If this is true...

708
01:08:32,734 --> 01:08:35,255
...you must be afraid of me, Vizier.

709
01:08:35,770 --> 01:08:37,810
Be afraid of me!

710
01:08:38,163 --> 01:08:41,174
No one will take Harmankaya from me!

711
01:08:41,499 --> 01:08:43,578
No one!

712
01:09:00,366 --> 01:09:02,566
Sergeant Ilgezdi!

713
01:09:05,642 --> 01:09:07,862
Where is Osman's head?

714
01:09:09,014 --> 01:09:13,694
Osman's head is still on his body.

715
01:09:15,166 --> 01:09:17,145
What does that mean?

716
01:09:17,356 --> 01:09:19,716
This is not our agreement, Geyhatu.

717
01:09:20,930 --> 01:09:23,920
A Turkmen named Turgut...

718
01:09:23,920 --> 01:09:27,470
...and a Lord named Kosses...

719
01:09:28,006 --> 01:09:32,145
...saved him from getting crushed
under my horses.

720
01:09:33,857 --> 01:09:36,657
You know them, Alam Shah.

721
01:09:39,163 --> 01:09:41,033
Kosses!

722
01:09:42,719 --> 01:09:44,569
Stupid Nikola!

723
01:09:46,350 --> 01:09:48,250
What's going to happen now?

724
01:09:50,238 --> 01:09:55,188
Sometimes only the horse knows
where he is going.

725
01:09:58,459 --> 01:10:02,289
Osman's horse is taking him to his end.

726
01:10:03,638 --> 01:10:06,518
Trouble waits for him in Konya.

727
01:10:16,956 --> 01:10:18,416
You!

728
01:10:19,173 --> 01:10:21,473
Selman, the Aide of Sultan.

729
01:10:22,447 --> 01:10:24,677
What are you doing here?

730
01:10:25,150 --> 01:10:27,310
I swear on Gok Tengri(Turkish God)...

731
01:10:27,795 --> 01:10:30,765
You think I am the aide of Sultan, but...

732
01:10:30,880 --> 01:10:35,100
I become the one whom Geyhatu wants
me to become.

733
01:10:38,248 --> 01:10:41,078
His commands are superior.

734
01:11:07,846 --> 01:11:09,806
Osman's dagger.

735
01:11:11,073 --> 01:11:16,553
I am sure that it shed so much blood.

736
01:11:28,163 --> 01:11:32,183
Now this will bring Osman's end.

737
01:11:48,575 --> 01:11:50,525
It's enough Gündüz!

738
01:11:50,599 --> 01:11:52,899
I can't go on like this!

739
01:11:54,269 --> 01:11:56,779
Gunduz!
What happened to you?

740
01:11:57,162 --> 01:11:59,022
What is up with you?

741
01:11:59,657 --> 01:12:05,207
How could you exile Selcan Hatun, whom
you consider as a mother, and your sisters?

742
01:12:07,000 --> 01:12:09,590
I had to for the peace of the tribe, Ayse.

743
01:12:10,483 --> 01:12:12,023
They needed to go.

744
01:12:12,969 --> 01:12:16,039
They were going to divide the
tribe if they were here.

745
01:12:17,190 --> 01:12:19,970
You keep talking about the peace
of the tribe.

746
01:12:20,372 --> 01:12:24,682
Do you do what you do for
the peace of our tribe?

747
01:12:26,499 --> 01:12:28,779
Or it's just your benefits?

748
01:12:31,299 --> 01:12:33,539
I don't know, Gunduz?

749
01:12:33,966 --> 01:12:36,186
What is your tongue talking about, Hatun?!

750
01:12:36,802 --> 01:12:39,922
When have I ever
looked after my own benefits?

751
01:12:41,911 --> 01:12:43,989
I only care the tribe's peace.

752
01:12:43,989 --> 01:12:47,669
I don't know who you are anymore Gunduz,
since the day you sit on this throne.

753
01:12:48,213 --> 01:12:52,553
You do what Vizier says
instead of saving your brother.

754
01:12:52,767 --> 01:12:56,527
Now you exile Osman Bey's
family...

755
01:12:57,228 --> 01:12:58,908
...and your mother!

756
01:12:59,636 --> 01:13:01,906
You divide the tribe!

757
01:13:02,516 --> 01:13:04,486
Notice it already!

758
01:13:07,248 --> 01:13:09,698
You are my Hatun!

759
01:13:13,296 --> 01:13:17,666
Your place is not against me!

760
01:13:19,263 --> 01:13:20,903
Your place is beside me!

761
01:13:23,585 --> 01:13:27,915
Questioning the command of Bey
is not your business!

762
01:13:29,571 --> 01:13:34,551
My business is to stand with
the truht, Gunduz Bey.

763
01:13:36,161 --> 01:13:39,969
If I don't sstand against you
when you are in the wrong way...

764
01:13:41,612 --> 01:13:43,562
...I cannot explain it in the afterlife.

765
01:13:46,724 --> 01:13:50,464
How are you going to
talk to your brother Osman Bey...

766
01:13:51,348 --> 01:13:53,228
...when he comes here?

767
01:13:54,002 --> 01:13:55,602
Think about that.

768
01:14:10,907 --> 01:14:13,857
O the holy of holies!
My Creator.

769
01:14:15,070 --> 01:14:18,700
You are the One who sees everything...

770
01:14:19,271 --> 01:14:21,371
...knows everything.

771
01:14:22,769 --> 01:14:25,209
You are paramount.

772
01:14:25,457 --> 01:14:27,117
For the sake of your messenger...

773
01:14:27,914 --> 01:14:33,927
...our prophet Hadrat Mohammed
“May Allah honor him and grant him peace”

774
01:14:36,087 --> 01:14:40,627
For the sake of Your messengers,
Your saints.

775
01:14:42,003 --> 01:14:46,743
For the sake of your humans
whose blood dripped on the ground...

776
01:14:47,250 --> 01:14:51,990
...in the aim of expanding your words.

777
01:14:54,786 --> 01:14:56,776
Let us avenge...

778
01:14:58,479 --> 01:15:01,469
for my brother Goktug...

779
01:15:02,691 --> 01:15:04,871
...and all the martyrs.

780
01:15:08,841 --> 01:15:10,451
O Allah.

781
01:15:11,720 --> 01:15:13,290
O Allah.

782
01:15:14,373 --> 01:15:16,203
You are the judge.

783
01:15:16,634 --> 01:15:18,544
You are the adjudicator

784
01:15:19,072 --> 01:15:21,632
You are the one who
separates good from bad...

785
01:15:21,632 --> 01:15:24,104
and vanity from the truth.

786
01:15:25,577 --> 01:15:27,017
O Allah.

787
01:15:28,383 --> 01:15:31,673
You spoil the tricks of the
oppressors, my Allah.

788
01:15:32,482 --> 01:15:37,732
Protect us from every
trouble that befalls us.

789
01:15:38,663 --> 01:15:41,893
Protect us from oppressors, my Allah.

790
01:15:44,170 --> 01:15:46,060
O Allah.

791
01:15:49,790 --> 01:15:51,550
Keep our feet steady...

792
01:15:53,189 --> 01:15:55,779
on the path we walk for you.

793
01:15:56,773 --> 01:15:59,643
O my guardian, my Allah.

794
01:16:03,417 --> 01:16:05,077
Amen.

795
01:16:14,979 --> 01:16:17,379
The soldiers are ready. We can set off.

796
01:16:20,275 --> 01:16:22,290
Can I come in, my Grand Vizier?

797
01:16:22,290 --> 01:16:23,840
Come.

798
01:16:28,609 --> 01:16:30,869
Landlord Nikola is here, Hadhrat
Grand Vizier.

799
01:16:38,532 --> 01:16:40,442
Grand Vizier Alemşah.

800
01:16:40,479 --> 01:16:42,249
I have something to say.

801
01:16:43,191 --> 01:16:45,601
Is there any news from Kosses?

802
01:16:45,690 --> 01:16:48,919
Kosses is now waiting in the dungeon
for the day he will be judged.

803
01:16:48,919 --> 01:16:51,129
He is in the past now.

804
01:16:51,473 --> 01:16:53,393
I'm talking about the future.

805
01:16:54,204 --> 01:16:55,664
The future?

806
01:16:56,351 --> 01:16:57,912
I'll listen to you, Nikola.

807
01:16:57,912 --> 01:17:00,052
What I will tell will benefit not only
me...

808
01:17:00,224 --> 01:17:05,071
but also you as long as you are with me,
Grand Vizier Alemşah. because...

809
01:17:05,071 --> 01:17:06,071
it's about the gold.

810
01:17:06,071 --> 01:17:08,751
I'm thinking of moving part of
the market to Harmankaya.

811
01:17:08,770 --> 01:17:11,470
I will lower the taxes too and thus...

812
01:17:12,295 --> 01:17:14,095
increase our profits.

813
01:17:23,391 --> 01:17:26,831
You are responsible for Harmankaya now.

814
01:17:27,771 --> 01:17:33,311
You can set up a market wherever you
want and sell whatever you want, Nikola.

815
01:17:34,947 --> 01:17:37,927
I love to do what I want.

816
01:17:39,684 --> 01:17:42,334
I'm glad that there is no problem
for you.

817
01:17:43,474 --> 01:17:46,784
The castle will gain the glory
it deserves...

818
01:17:46,946 --> 01:17:50,356
in the hands of a skillful
landlord like you, Nikola.

819
01:17:52,784 --> 01:17:55,684
It was damaged when Kosses
was responsible for the castle.

820
01:17:56,414 --> 01:18:00,034
Both the castle and Kosses will get
what they deserve.

821
01:18:01,799 --> 01:18:03,369
Won't they?

822
01:18:03,974 --> 01:18:06,074
As someone rises...

823
01:18:08,289 --> 01:18:10,399
someone falls.

824
01:18:11,116 --> 01:18:12,546
It's natural.

825
01:18:12,727 --> 01:18:14,627
It's the law of the jungle.

826
01:18:15,409 --> 01:18:18,259
-With your permission.
-Goodbye, Nikola.

827
01:18:23,033 --> 01:18:25,053
Goodbye.

828
01:18:26,671 --> 01:18:29,091
Kosses was never been in Constantine.

829
01:18:29,470 --> 01:18:32,580
He is lying. Why don't we punish
him, my Grand Vizier?

830
01:18:33,231 --> 01:18:35,711
Everything has its time, Konur.

831
01:18:36,002 --> 01:18:38,752
When the time comes, we will ask
for the account.

832
01:18:40,093 --> 01:18:43,343
When we give the castle to
Gündüz Bey...

833
01:18:44,368 --> 01:18:47,168
the account will already be asked.

834
01:18:48,450 --> 01:18:50,620
Nikola will get so angry.

835
01:18:51,710 --> 01:18:53,660
I gave the castle to him.

836
01:18:54,184 --> 01:18:56,574
And the one who will
take it back is also me.

837
01:18:59,280 --> 01:19:02,310
Let's made him think that
we believe him for now.

838
01:19:03,927 --> 01:19:07,737
What's important is the
strength of Gündüz.

839
01:19:09,126 --> 01:19:10,996
So, the strength of mine.

840
01:19:13,800 --> 01:19:17,280
What is the Grand Vizier planning?

841
01:19:17,317 --> 01:19:20,157
Will the Grand Vizier
give Harmankaya to the Turks?

842
01:19:21,653 --> 01:19:24,563
I don't give what is mine to
anyone, Argos.

843
01:19:27,352 --> 01:19:29,372
Harmankaya is mine.

844
01:19:30,154 --> 01:19:34,084
If the Vizier makes the mistake
of giving it to Gündüz Bey...

845
01:19:34,700 --> 01:19:38,490
it will not be easy for him at all.

846
01:19:45,142 --> 01:19:48,852
Increase the number
of soldiers in Harmankaya.

847
01:19:49,058 --> 01:19:51,978
But the Vizier shouldn't know this.

848
01:19:52,695 --> 01:19:55,015
He is a Turk, after all.

849
01:19:55,597 --> 01:19:58,747
Don't trust a Turk Argus, never and ever.

850
01:19:58,933 --> 01:20:00,573
Especially a Turk like him.

851
01:20:01,618 --> 01:20:03,578
Harmankaya.

852
01:20:04,050 --> 01:20:06,510
I will not give it that easily.

853
01:20:10,617 --> 01:20:12,787
My son, who makes me happy with one look.

854
01:20:13,572 --> 01:20:16,112
Your presence gives me strength, my Orhan.

855
01:20:28,802 --> 01:20:31,372
Alps and Bacıs are ready.

856
01:20:33,020 --> 01:20:36,320
No one will be able to touch that hide
until my Bey comes.

857
01:20:40,419 --> 01:20:44,509
Let's go. Let's take the hide that belongs
to Osman Bey back from Gündüz Bey.

858
01:20:58,171 --> 01:21:02,041
Gündüz got up in anger and
he will sit down with a loss.

859
01:21:02,956 --> 01:21:05,536
If this goes on, blood will be shed.

860
01:21:05,844 --> 01:21:08,514
Why don't we talk for the last time?

861
01:21:09,938 --> 01:21:12,898
Gündüz Bey's
ears have become deaf to the truth.

862
01:21:13,788 --> 01:21:17,888
You also know that once an
ear is deaf to the truth...

863
01:21:18,570 --> 01:21:20,250
it is beyond hope.

864
01:21:20,893 --> 01:21:23,536
Mother, we don't want a slaughter too.

865
01:21:23,536 --> 01:21:26,686
Gündüz Bey will see our
seriousness and withdraw.

866
01:21:27,792 --> 01:21:30,222
What if he doesn't
because of his stubbornness?

867
01:21:31,002 --> 01:21:32,972
What if he doesn't withdraw?

868
01:21:34,902 --> 01:21:37,102
Then the blood will be shed, mother.

869
01:21:51,583 --> 01:21:53,403
The time has come.

870
01:21:56,409 --> 01:21:59,229
I hope they understand the truth...

871
01:22:00,364 --> 01:22:02,484
and go easily.

872
01:22:03,250 --> 01:22:05,630
Don't make it difficult for me, my Allah.

873
01:22:07,410 --> 01:22:10,790
Don't make me do things that
I don't want, my Allah.

874
01:22:13,690 --> 01:22:15,630
Can I come in, my Bey?

875
01:22:16,709 --> 01:22:18,229
Come.

876
01:22:22,801 --> 01:22:24,421
My Bey.

877
01:22:24,753 --> 01:22:28,812
As you said, I went to the tents of
Hatuns. But all of them are in...

878
01:22:28,812 --> 01:22:30,142
the tent of Malhun Hatun.

879
01:22:30,142 --> 01:22:30,820
The time has come but they don't
seem like they will leave.
the tent of Malhun Hatun.

880
01:22:30,820 --> 01:22:33,382
The time has come but they don't
seem like they will leave.

881
01:22:34,869 --> 01:22:36,809
Time is up.

882
01:22:39,414 --> 01:22:42,314
Since they don't take the easy way,..

883
01:22:46,110 --> 01:22:48,500
take the horses and go to their tents.

884
01:22:50,019 --> 01:22:51,649
Gündüz Bey!

885
01:22:57,037 --> 01:23:01,437
You forced us to leave
but we're not going anywhere!

886
01:23:05,596 --> 01:23:08,396
If you have the courage, get
out of your tent!

887
01:23:18,954 --> 01:23:20,684
Hatuns!

888
01:23:21,657 --> 01:23:24,027
The time I gave you is up.

889
01:23:25,237 --> 01:23:27,347
Why are you still here?

890
01:23:29,978 --> 01:23:31,988
It's the order of your Bey.

891
01:23:32,154 --> 01:23:33,549
Will you go against this?!

892
01:23:33,549 --> 01:23:36,819
We are here to follow our Bey's order.

893
01:23:37,422 --> 01:23:41,532
With the order of Osman Bey, we are
here to bring you down.

894
01:23:43,447 --> 01:23:46,707
What you are doing means
making mischief.

895
01:23:47,598 --> 01:23:53,364
Go duly without taking the arrow out of
the bow by tempting people, Malhun Hatun.

896
01:23:53,364 --> 01:23:57,634
We are not going anywhere.
If you can, prevent us!

897
01:23:58,829 --> 01:24:00,519
Bala Hatun.

898
01:24:01,310 --> 01:24:03,030
At least you don't do this.

899
01:24:03,813 --> 01:24:07,883
Go in silence or something bad is
going to happen.

900
01:24:08,086 --> 01:24:10,166
You don't do this, Gündüz Bey.

901
01:24:10,280 --> 01:24:12,390
The Bey of the Kayı Tribe is Osman Bey.

902
01:24:12,686 --> 01:24:14,576
And it's his order.

903
01:24:21,752 --> 01:24:23,312
Mother.

904
01:24:31,732 --> 01:24:33,812
If you don't listen to me...

905
01:24:36,219 --> 01:24:38,409
then I'm not responsible
for what I will do.

906
01:24:42,582 --> 01:24:44,122
Alps!

907
01:24:46,608 --> 01:24:48,478
Stand at attention.

908
01:25:05,836 --> 01:25:07,626
I am Malhun Hatun!

909
01:25:07,874 --> 01:25:09,854
I am Osman Bey's Hatun!

910
01:25:10,672 --> 01:25:15,162
If there is an Alp who will draw a sword
at me, let him act now!

911
01:25:16,781 --> 01:25:21,431
Alps! Be careful who you draw a sword.

912
01:25:26,843 --> 01:25:31,053
There are Osman Bey's Hatuns
in front of you!

913
01:25:33,646 --> 01:25:37,752
How quickly have you forgotten the days
when you use your...

914
01:25:37,752 --> 01:25:39,092
swords behind Osman Bey?

915
01:25:39,092 --> 01:25:42,282
Is what you're doing worthy
of being an Alp?

916
01:25:58,983 --> 01:26:00,313
Alps!

917
01:26:03,662 --> 01:26:06,002
If they are Osman Bey's Hatuns...

918
01:26:08,276 --> 01:26:11,416
I am the son of Ertuğrul Ghazi, Gündüz Bey!

919
01:26:17,352 --> 01:26:19,382
It's the order of the Bey of Kayı.

920
01:26:19,435 --> 01:26:21,175
Stand at attention!

921
01:27:36,422 --> 01:27:38,142
Gündüz Bey.

922
01:27:38,655 --> 01:27:40,195
Malhun Hatun.

923
01:27:42,166 --> 01:27:43,766
What is going on here?

924
01:27:44,276 --> 01:27:46,446
Put down your swords.

925
01:28:13,628 --> 01:28:15,448
The time has come.

926
01:28:16,344 --> 01:28:21,134
Now both the white and the
black ones will be revealed.

927
01:28:21,866 --> 01:28:23,286
For sure.

928
01:28:24,427 --> 01:28:27,607
I will wait for you at the closest
place to the palace, Osman Bey.

929
01:28:27,669 --> 01:28:30,629
I will always be ready, don't worry.

930
01:28:31,962 --> 01:28:33,822
Thank you, Kosses.

931
01:28:33,855 --> 01:28:37,305
I will not forget what you did. You
acted truthfully.

932
01:28:37,991 --> 01:28:40,631
After all you've done for me...

933
01:28:40,753 --> 01:28:43,513
let me do this at least, Osman Bey.

934
01:28:45,755 --> 01:28:47,285
Thank you.

935
01:28:48,514 --> 01:28:50,724
We will lead with Alps.

936
01:28:50,877 --> 01:28:53,647
When you come we will be
in the palace Osman Bey.

937
01:28:54,148 --> 01:28:55,888
Alright, Turgut Bey.

938
01:28:56,669 --> 01:28:58,259
We are going, Alps.

939
01:29:04,723 --> 01:29:06,043
Tuğra Han.

940
01:29:08,302 --> 01:29:11,232
You will be on the alert here with Kosses.

941
01:29:11,420 --> 01:29:13,000
As you ordered, my Bey.

942
01:29:14,066 --> 01:29:16,046
Take care of yourself.

943
01:29:16,299 --> 01:29:17,989
Thank you.

944
01:29:24,506 --> 01:29:27,946
Whatever Gündüz Bey is doing, he is
doing it for his tribe.

945
01:29:29,155 --> 01:29:33,055
Did we do bad by putting Gündüz Bey
in charge?

946
01:29:36,339 --> 01:29:39,729
Doesn't Gündüz Bey have the right
to sit on the hide?

947
01:29:45,908 --> 01:29:49,608
Aren't Gündüz Bey the son
of Ertuğrul Gazi too?

948
01:29:56,517 --> 01:30:00,127
Your Bey wants Osman Bey's Hatuns to
go to prevent making mischief...

949
01:30:00,664 --> 01:30:05,364
and these kinds of events.

950
01:30:06,761 --> 01:30:08,561
Who make mischief is you.

951
01:30:09,362 --> 01:30:13,972
You are the one who wants to ignore the
owner of the hide and set up a nativity.

952
01:30:14,773 --> 01:30:17,573
Go inside the tent and look around,
Malhun Hatun.

953
01:30:17,752 --> 01:30:20,332
Is the owner of the hide sitting on
the hide?

954
01:30:21,539 --> 01:30:23,289
The previous owner of the hide is...

955
01:30:24,032 --> 01:30:27,232
waiting to be in the
presence of the Sultan now.

956
01:30:31,568 --> 01:30:34,258
You talk like you don't know,
Vizier Alemşah.

957
01:30:35,121 --> 01:30:39,351
You sent the owner of the hide
to Konya with lots of tricks.

958
01:30:40,162 --> 01:30:43,952
But don't worry. My Bey will reveal the
truth...

959
01:30:45,569 --> 01:30:47,529
and return to his tribe.

960
01:30:49,826 --> 01:30:52,476
You are misspeaking, Bala Hatun.

961
01:30:53,717 --> 01:30:56,047
I don't use tricks.

962
01:30:56,612 --> 01:30:59,702
I am here to maintain the order.

963
01:31:00,371 --> 01:31:04,481
I don't want to hurt anyone.

964
01:31:05,793 --> 01:31:07,353
But...

965
01:31:08,606 --> 01:31:13,616
if you intend to make
mischief between the people...

966
01:31:16,900 --> 01:31:20,360
I will have to do the things that I
don't want.

967
01:31:22,335 --> 01:31:26,345
Who are you kicking out of whose tribe?

968
01:31:29,367 --> 01:31:31,057
Gündüz Bey!

969
01:31:31,807 --> 01:31:34,087
Didn't you ever learn from your uncle?

970
01:31:37,451 --> 01:31:40,251
Don't do this mistake.

971
01:31:48,984 --> 01:31:51,644
Now, Hatuns.

972
01:31:52,814 --> 01:31:56,114
Get out of here without any problems.

973
01:31:57,134 --> 01:31:59,314
We are not going, Vizier!

974
01:32:00,015 --> 01:32:02,935
Come on! If you can, make us leave here!

975
01:32:03,506 --> 01:32:06,146
Whatever you do, we won't go
one step further!

976
01:32:34,733 --> 01:32:37,053
Who are you and what do you want?

977
01:32:38,223 --> 01:32:40,413
I am here to see Sultan Mesud.

978
01:32:42,702 --> 01:32:44,542
Inform the aide.

979
01:33:46,816 --> 01:33:48,556
Hatuns!

980
01:33:49,016 --> 01:33:52,636
Alps! Put your weapons down!

981
01:33:58,443 --> 01:34:02,063
An Alp of Kayı doesn't fight
with his brother!

982
01:34:03,700 --> 01:34:06,200
We will not fall into this trap!

983
01:34:06,823 --> 01:34:09,173
We will not shed brother blood.

984
01:34:10,914 --> 01:34:12,704
Come on!

985
01:34:30,993 --> 01:34:32,983
When you come here, I thought that...

986
01:34:33,774 --> 01:34:37,284
if Gündüz is still Gündüz that I know...

987
01:34:37,710 --> 01:34:40,980
he would not let anything like this happen.

988
01:34:42,461 --> 01:34:45,651
I thought he would withdraw and...

989
01:34:46,068 --> 01:34:49,708
show generosity when the time comes.

990
01:34:52,634 --> 01:34:54,244
But...

991
01:34:55,309 --> 01:34:58,219
either I have never known him or...

992
01:34:59,929 --> 01:35:04,659
Gunduz that I know vanished away.

993
01:35:13,480 --> 01:35:15,760
We won't let his happen!

994
01:35:16,514 --> 01:35:19,254
We won't spill the blood of our brothers!

995
01:35:20,171 --> 01:35:23,311
Therefore, now...

996
01:35:23,587 --> 01:35:28,297
...we are leaving our own tribe willingly.

997
01:35:29,840 --> 01:35:31,800
But...

998
01:35:33,730 --> 01:35:35,690
...when the day comes...

999
01:35:36,481 --> 01:35:39,401
...and the Bey of Kayı, Osman Bey...

1000
01:35:39,995 --> 01:35:42,245
...returns to his tribe...

1001
01:35:43,981 --> 01:35:49,131
...you will pay one by one for all
you have done.

1002
01:35:58,831 --> 01:36:00,301
Mother!

1003
01:36:01,047 --> 01:36:02,967
Now is not the time.

1004
01:36:03,916 --> 01:36:05,866
If we draw our swords now...

1005
01:36:07,002 --> 01:36:09,762
...we will be on a road of no return.

1006
01:36:12,499 --> 01:36:14,069
Come on, my girl.

1007
01:36:45,004 --> 01:36:46,644
You did the right thing, mother.

1008
01:36:49,682 --> 01:36:51,202
Thank you.

1009
01:37:10,572 --> 01:37:12,612
Take a good look at what you have done...

1010
01:37:13,089 --> 01:37:16,949
...to your own tribe with your own hands,
Gündüz.

1011
01:37:20,080 --> 01:37:23,930
I don't know how you trust his words.

1012
01:37:25,018 --> 01:37:27,158
But what I know is that...

1013
01:37:28,762 --> 01:37:31,082
...you became a stranger to your brother.

1014
01:37:31,968 --> 01:37:33,888
Don't do the same to your tribe.

1015
01:37:48,048 --> 01:37:50,398
Mother, bless your right.

1016
01:37:53,693 --> 01:37:56,153
I don't want you to leave here like this.

1017
01:37:57,959 --> 01:38:00,179
But there is nothing I can do.

1018
01:38:01,109 --> 01:38:02,809
I know, my girl.

1019
01:38:05,004 --> 01:38:08,234
I know, there is nothing you can do.

1020
01:38:10,619 --> 01:38:12,159
I bless my right.

1021
01:38:13,430 --> 01:38:16,660
Take care of yourself and your mind.

1022
01:38:22,536 --> 01:38:23,936
Come on!

1023
01:38:31,396 --> 01:38:33,216
Malhun Hatun!

1024
01:38:34,823 --> 01:38:39,293
Where are you taking Orhan, the heir of
Kayı Tribe?

1025
01:38:47,444 --> 01:38:50,934
Orhan belongs to the Kayı Tribe.

1026
01:39:23,416 --> 01:39:26,936
He didn't say who he is.
He wants to see the Sultan.

1027
01:39:30,459 --> 01:39:32,669
I will meet Sultan Mesud.

1028
01:39:33,640 --> 01:39:36,430
Who are you that Sultan accepts you
to his presence?

1029
01:39:38,130 --> 01:39:40,110
Who are you, man?

1030
01:39:45,079 --> 01:39:47,429
The Mighty Bey of these lands.

1031
01:39:50,842 --> 01:39:53,512
The border between Rum and Konya.

1032
01:39:56,794 --> 01:39:58,794
The protector of the Turkmens.

1033
01:40:00,947 --> 01:40:03,527
The Bey of Seljuk...

1034
01:40:05,038 --> 01:40:07,968
...Osman Bey, son of Ertuğrul Gazi.

1035
01:40:19,820 --> 01:40:21,870
Now you know who I am.

1036
01:40:22,768 --> 01:40:24,848
There was an order for my name.

1037
01:40:26,177 --> 01:40:28,257
I cam to surrender to the Sultan.

1038
01:40:34,334 --> 01:40:36,724
I will never leave my son to the traitors!

1039
01:40:37,081 --> 01:40:39,031
He belongs to his mother's side.

1040
01:40:44,664 --> 01:40:46,799
You are a bey daughter, Malhun Hatun.

1041
01:40:46,799 --> 01:40:48,459
You know the rules.

1042
01:40:49,511 --> 01:40:52,241
Orhan belongs to the Kayı Tribe.

1043
01:40:53,106 --> 01:40:55,226
Don't take one more step!

1044
01:40:58,476 --> 01:41:00,626
Orhan is entrusted to us by Osman Bey.

1045
01:41:00,698 --> 01:41:02,678
We left the tribe but...

1046
01:41:04,087 --> 01:41:07,237
...we won't leave him to anyone!
Orhan is coming with us.

1047
01:41:12,403 --> 01:41:14,307
Orhan should be with his mother!

1048
01:41:14,307 --> 01:41:16,477
You can't separate them!

1049
01:41:16,649 --> 01:41:18,639
Gündüz, do something!

1050
01:41:18,917 --> 01:41:21,476
Don't ever separate the child from his
mother.

1051
01:41:21,476 --> 01:41:23,426
Don't sin.

1052
01:41:25,763 --> 01:41:27,253
Gündüz?

1053
01:41:28,515 --> 01:41:31,275
Separating the child from his mother?

1054
01:41:31,762 --> 01:41:34,902
Who are you to dare that?

1055
01:41:35,282 --> 01:41:37,002
Selcen Hatun...

1056
01:41:37,176 --> 01:41:39,216
...you know the rules too.

1057
01:41:39,948 --> 01:41:41,488
Don't make this harder.

1058
01:41:42,387 --> 01:41:44,427
Am I wrong, Kayı Tribe?

1059
01:41:45,017 --> 01:41:46,657
Tell me.

1060
01:41:46,931 --> 01:41:50,541
Isn't Orhan Osman Bey's blood?

1061
01:41:53,397 --> 01:41:57,967
Kayı Tribe is the safest place for Orhan.

1062
01:42:04,721 --> 01:42:06,801
Hatuns...

1063
01:42:07,455 --> 01:42:12,315
....leave Orhan to us and leave quietly.

1064
01:42:14,682 --> 01:42:16,751
I'd rather die!

1065
01:42:16,751 --> 01:42:20,261
We will die and kill for Orhan. Get out of
our way so we can leave!

1066
01:42:29,880 --> 01:42:34,350
Aide Selman will inform the Sultan that
you are here, Osman Bey.

1067
01:42:34,541 --> 01:42:36,271
Don't worry.

1068
01:42:38,103 --> 01:42:39,973
I don't.

1069
01:42:42,252 --> 01:42:43,682
I am waiting.

1070
01:43:12,576 --> 01:43:13,936
My Sultan...

1071
01:43:14,854 --> 01:43:16,614
...the Bey of Kayı, Osman Bey...

1072
01:43:17,068 --> 01:43:18,768
...surrendered.

1073
01:43:19,951 --> 01:43:23,241
So, Sergeant İlgezdi brought him.

1074
01:43:24,129 --> 01:43:26,119
Bring him to me, immediately.

1075
01:43:26,792 --> 01:43:30,102
My Sultan, Osman Bey was alone.

1076
01:43:41,442 --> 01:43:42,972
Vizier Alemşah...

1077
01:43:45,997 --> 01:43:47,717
...this is not the way to do it.

1078
01:43:48,504 --> 01:43:50,534
Don't separate Orhan from his mother.

1079
01:43:51,722 --> 01:43:53,562
He is too little.

1080
01:43:55,493 --> 01:43:59,073
Orhan belongs to the Kayı Tribe.
This is the rule.

1081
01:44:05,661 --> 01:44:07,711
Ayşe, take Orhan.

1082
01:44:20,333 --> 01:44:22,173
Don't get close, Ayşe Hatun!

1083
01:44:22,751 --> 01:44:24,371
Don't!

1084
01:44:41,264 --> 01:44:42,724
Mother!

1085
01:44:43,472 --> 01:44:45,782
Mother, please don't ask this from me!

1086
01:44:45,900 --> 01:44:47,580
Patience, my girl.

1087
01:44:47,965 --> 01:44:49,745
We will be patient.

1088
01:44:51,018 --> 01:44:52,908
His foster mother is here.

1089
01:44:53,807 --> 01:44:56,167
Ayşe will take great care of Orhan too.

1090
01:45:00,680 --> 01:45:03,180
-Come on, my girl.
-Mother!

1091
01:45:03,267 --> 01:45:05,257
My Orhan is just a baby.

1092
01:45:05,525 --> 01:45:07,195
No!

1093
01:45:08,172 --> 01:45:09,822
My boy...

1094
01:45:09,822 --> 01:45:12,842
...is having his trial when he is just
a baby.

1095
01:45:12,992 --> 01:45:15,412
He will be brave like his father.

1096
01:45:15,787 --> 01:45:18,417
Come on, Malhun.
Come on, my girl.

1097
01:45:23,258 --> 01:45:25,058
Bala!

1098
01:45:30,637 --> 01:45:32,897
Ayşe, come here.

1099
01:45:40,584 --> 01:45:41,824
Aygül.

1100
01:45:52,255 --> 01:45:56,335
Too much blood will be shed. Osman would
want this too.

1101
01:45:56,824 --> 01:45:59,054
Let's not make a family fight.

1102
01:46:05,707 --> 01:46:09,437
You will pay for this when Osman returns!

1103
01:47:23,704 --> 01:47:27,934
I swear to Allah, I will protect him with
my life.

1104
01:48:08,543 --> 01:48:10,223
Come on, my girl.

1105
01:48:31,448 --> 01:48:33,348
Malhun, my girl!

1106
01:48:38,178 --> 01:48:40,618
The day for justice will come, Gündüz Bey.

1107
01:48:41,063 --> 01:48:44,063
Until that day, do whatever you want.

1108
01:48:45,142 --> 01:48:49,352
But when that day comes, I will be
right on your neck.

1109
01:48:51,216 --> 01:48:53,596
All Kayı Tribe is my witness that...

1110
01:48:53,663 --> 01:48:57,893
...you will pay for separating me
from my tribe...

1111
01:48:58,655 --> 01:49:02,345
...from my child!

1112
01:49:29,604 --> 01:49:33,864
I hope your blind eyes open soon so you
can see the truth.

1113
01:49:35,159 --> 01:49:37,869
Otherwise, you will regret it so much.

1114
01:49:38,091 --> 01:49:41,371
But it will be too late.

1115
01:49:42,630 --> 01:49:45,140
These are my last words to you.

1116
01:50:28,225 --> 01:50:29,825
Ferman.

1117
01:50:32,615 --> 01:50:37,455
These three hatuns will die before
they become trouble.

1118
01:50:40,548 --> 01:50:44,908
Kayı Tribe will have infinite peace.

1119
01:50:45,677 --> 01:50:47,307
As you order, my Vizier.

1120
01:51:21,438 --> 01:51:23,968
When will this persecution of
the Turks end?

1121
01:51:24,179 --> 01:51:26,539
Tyrants are in the heart of the state.

1122
01:51:31,948 --> 01:51:36,028
For now, they believe the right thing
to do is to bow.

1123
01:51:37,284 --> 01:51:41,144
Right is known as wrong and the wrong
is known as right.

1124
01:51:42,396 --> 01:51:46,446
You made the right decision by sending
the hatuns to exile.

1125
01:51:47,556 --> 01:51:50,436
It was necessary for the unity
of the tribe.

1126
01:51:52,991 --> 01:51:57,041
You behaved in a manner befitting a Bey.

1127
01:51:59,001 --> 01:52:02,041
Everything I do is for the tribe.

1128
01:52:04,944 --> 01:52:07,284
This was necessary, so I did.

1129
01:52:08,469 --> 01:52:11,669
But, Vizier Alemşah...

1130
01:52:12,762 --> 01:52:15,452
...why did we separate Orhan
from his mother?

1131
01:52:20,125 --> 01:52:24,965
Of course, I don't want to separate
a child from his mother too, Gündüz Bey.

1132
01:52:25,978 --> 01:52:29,408
But the Turk's tradition is this.

1133
01:52:30,900 --> 01:52:34,720
His tribe is the safest place for Orhan.

1134
01:52:36,007 --> 01:52:37,627
You are right.

1135
01:52:37,958 --> 01:52:39,798
It's the rule.

1136
01:52:40,555 --> 01:52:44,735
Orhan is entrusted to me by my brother.

1137
01:52:46,057 --> 01:52:48,847
May Allah protect but if something
happened to him there...

1138
01:52:49,162 --> 01:52:51,392
...we can't look at Osman's face again.

1139
01:52:53,480 --> 01:52:56,770
A great conquest now befits...

1140
01:52:56,825 --> 01:52:59,615
...a Bey of foresight like you.

1141
01:53:02,859 --> 01:53:05,139
Get ready, Gündüz Bey.

1142
01:53:05,721 --> 01:53:08,461
We will conquer the Castle of Harmankaya.

1143
01:53:10,690 --> 01:53:13,680
All the treasure will be Kayı's.

1144
01:53:15,283 --> 01:53:20,673
The lands that Osman killed many alps
for the sake of but could not conquer...

1145
01:53:21,945 --> 01:53:25,085
...will be yours without even touching
your sword.

1146
01:53:26,396 --> 01:53:30,206
So, Kayı Flag will take its place...

1147
01:53:30,443 --> 01:53:33,113
...at the Castle of Harmankaya, right?

1148
01:53:34,987 --> 01:53:37,017
Right, Gündüz Bey.

1149
01:53:38,026 --> 01:53:41,896
Conquest without bloodshed through
peace...

1150
01:53:42,095 --> 01:53:44,375
...is the most blessed.

1151
01:53:45,281 --> 01:53:50,001
Our intention was to give Harmankaya to
the Kayı without bloodshed...

1152
01:53:50,521 --> 01:53:53,381
...from the beginning.

1153
01:53:53,749 --> 01:53:57,629
But rebellious Osman couldn't see this.

1154
01:53:59,225 --> 01:54:02,175
Now, conquering
the Castle of Harmankaya...

1155
01:54:02,513 --> 01:54:05,003
...will be your fate, I hope.

1156
01:54:07,604 --> 01:54:12,144
The Tribe and Söğüt will benefit greatly
from this.

1157
01:54:13,319 --> 01:54:15,729
Everyone will receive peace.

1158
01:54:16,623 --> 01:54:18,423
I hope, Vizier Alemşah.

1159
01:54:18,628 --> 01:54:20,148
I hope.

1160
01:54:23,340 --> 01:54:26,080
You will win too, Gündüz Bey.

1161
01:54:27,153 --> 01:54:29,673
With the conquest of Harmankaya...

1162
01:54:30,630 --> 01:54:34,730
...no one but you will get close to
this throne.

1163
01:54:38,227 --> 01:54:43,117
When you go to the Bey Assembly with
the conquest of Harmankaya...

1164
01:54:44,241 --> 01:54:49,731
...other Beys will take it upon themselves
not to seat anyone but you on this throne.

1165
01:55:31,996 --> 01:55:33,646
My Sultan.

1166
01:55:40,447 --> 01:55:43,657
Osman Bey whom I know as the Mighty
Bey of these lands...

1167
01:55:47,363 --> 01:55:51,323
...is now in front of me as a rebel.

1168
01:55:52,730 --> 01:55:54,520
Never.

1169
01:55:55,427 --> 01:55:57,547
Never, my Sultan.

1170
01:55:59,680 --> 01:56:02,180
I have always been loyal to you.

1171
01:56:05,875 --> 01:56:07,085
But...

1172
01:56:10,116 --> 01:56:11,906
...if you let me...

1173
01:56:15,144 --> 01:56:17,484
...I would like to explain myself.

1174
01:56:26,953 --> 01:56:31,803
I have been reading this over and over
again since the day it arrived, Osman.

1175
01:56:34,116 --> 01:56:36,896
I look for one lie in it.

1176
01:56:47,182 --> 01:56:48,762
Tell me, Osman.

1177
01:56:49,707 --> 01:56:51,037
Tell me.

1178
01:56:51,641 --> 01:56:56,631
Relieve the trust you broke.

1179
01:56:59,487 --> 01:57:03,457
But first, start with telling...

1180
01:57:04,093 --> 01:57:06,253
...where the Sergeant İlgezdi is.

1181
01:57:20,534 --> 01:57:23,714
They will pay for taking my son from me!

1182
01:57:27,526 --> 01:57:29,746
Do we deserve these, mother?

1183
01:57:31,680 --> 01:57:35,370
Malhun Hatun, Ayşe Hatun will take good
care of Orhan.

1184
01:57:36,688 --> 01:57:39,578
You will get your son back, Malhun Hatun.

1185
01:57:40,568 --> 01:57:42,608
I hope.

1186
01:57:45,529 --> 01:57:49,139
Blood will be shed. Too much blood
will be shed!

1187
01:57:49,422 --> 01:57:52,992
After this last thing he did!

1188
01:57:53,377 --> 01:57:55,547
How will he redeem from this?

1189
01:57:55,598 --> 01:57:57,138
It's our fault!

1190
01:57:57,138 --> 01:58:00,508
We shouldn't have left Orhan there!

1191
01:58:00,919 --> 01:58:02,959
Enough, Aygül!

1192
01:58:02,987 --> 01:58:06,607
We left Orhan there so as to not spill
the blood of our brothers and sisters!

1193
01:58:08,977 --> 01:58:10,797
Orhan is in his tribe.

1194
01:58:11,314 --> 01:58:13,384
Not in the hands of the enemy.

1195
01:58:15,695 --> 01:58:19,965
Besides, don't you see what Vizier is
trying to do?

1196
01:58:21,443 --> 01:58:24,733
He wanted to paint us as rebels and
himself right.

1197
01:58:25,254 --> 01:58:27,244
But he couldn't.

1198
01:58:28,704 --> 01:58:32,914
We would be wrong in the eyes of
the people if the blood was shed.

1199
01:58:38,492 --> 01:58:40,802
This is why I separated you from your son.

1200
01:58:43,806 --> 01:58:46,086
Bless your right, my child.

1201
01:58:48,382 --> 01:58:50,292
If we had drew the swords...

1202
01:58:51,379 --> 01:58:54,119
...we would be on a road of no return.

1203
01:58:55,547 --> 01:58:57,337
I bless, mother.

1204
01:58:57,637 --> 01:58:59,777
You thought right.

1205
01:59:02,708 --> 01:59:05,628
Being a mother is something different,
Malhun Hatun.

1206
01:59:06,329 --> 01:59:09,059
Being apart from your child is too.

1207
01:59:15,719 --> 01:59:17,969
But you are a strong Hatun.

1208
01:59:18,464 --> 01:59:20,594
You didn't fall for the Vizier's game.

1209
01:59:35,831 --> 01:59:40,021
Why would Geyhatu attack my soldier,
Osman?

1210
01:59:42,169 --> 01:59:44,209
How do we know it was not you?

1211
01:59:47,803 --> 01:59:50,593
If I would kill Sergeant İlgezdi...

1212
01:59:51,896 --> 01:59:54,116
...I would do it to escape.

1213
01:59:58,215 --> 01:59:59,605
My Sultan...

1214
02:00:01,213 --> 02:00:03,083
...here I am.

1215
02:00:04,251 --> 02:00:06,741
I am right in front of you.

1216
02:00:10,853 --> 02:00:12,133
Geyhatu.

1217
02:00:13,791 --> 02:00:15,621
Geyhatu, huh?

1218
02:00:15,622 --> 02:00:16,792
Why?

1219
02:00:17,985 --> 02:00:21,855
Geyhatu didn't attack Seljuk...

1220
02:00:25,139 --> 02:00:27,199
...he attacked me.

1221
02:00:30,440 --> 02:00:35,190
Sergeant İlgezdi was martyred there so as
not to give...

1222
02:00:36,473 --> 02:00:38,513
...me and my alps.

1223
02:00:42,649 --> 02:00:45,759
Are you that of an important person,
Osman?

1224
02:00:49,770 --> 02:00:52,440
Geyhatu wants to take your life...

1225
02:00:52,536 --> 02:00:55,396
...and İlgezdi sacrifices his life
for you.

1226
02:00:58,336 --> 02:01:00,616
Geyhatu is my ally.

1227
02:01:02,031 --> 02:01:04,821
Why would he try to kill someone
coming to me?

1228
02:01:05,790 --> 02:01:09,230
Also when, the coming one is an arrested
criminal.

1229
02:01:12,726 --> 02:01:14,366
My Sultan...

1230
02:01:18,306 --> 02:01:21,906
...there are so many people you know
as your ally.

1231
02:01:24,806 --> 02:01:27,896
The reason why they stay behind you is...

1232
02:01:31,226 --> 02:01:33,776
...that they make their plans easily
this way.

1233
02:01:42,007 --> 02:01:44,257
I am not behind you...

1234
02:01:47,356 --> 02:01:49,016
...I am by your side.

1235
02:01:52,219 --> 02:01:54,379
I have no secrets.

1236
02:01:55,687 --> 02:01:57,127
But...

1237
02:01:59,078 --> 02:02:01,798
...take a good look at the people
behind you.

1238
02:02:06,843 --> 02:02:09,093
If you don't hide anything...

1239
02:02:10,996 --> 02:02:12,836
...if you don't have any secret...

1240
02:02:13,775 --> 02:02:16,005
...then speak openly too, Osman Bey.

1241
02:02:56,134 --> 02:02:57,864
-Aaaaa!
-Bala!

1242
02:02:57,956 --> 02:03:01,126
-I have pain!
-Alps, stop!

1243
02:03:02,076 --> 02:03:04,646
-Mother!
-Are you all right, my girl?

1244
02:03:04,711 --> 02:03:05,747
Bala!

1245
02:03:05,747 --> 02:03:07,696
I thought it would go away but it
didn't!

1246
02:03:07,696 --> 02:03:08,866
Bala!

1247
02:03:09,003 --> 02:03:11,913
It is our lucky day, Julia.

1248
02:03:12,185 --> 02:03:14,245
We will kill them all.

1249
02:03:14,472 --> 02:03:16,582
No one will be left alive.

1250
02:03:19,651 --> 02:03:23,871
I will kill that pregnant one
with my own hands.

1251
02:03:25,016 --> 02:03:27,213
How long have you been in pain?

1252
02:03:27,213 --> 02:03:29,037
Mother, what if she gives birth now?

1253
02:03:29,037 --> 02:03:31,627
Stop, girl!
How long have you been in pain?

1254
02:03:31,826 --> 02:03:34,846
Since yesterday right? You were touching
your stomach yesterday.

1255
02:03:34,942 --> 02:03:38,312
I waited for it to end but it got
stronger, mother!

1256
02:03:38,498 --> 02:03:41,027
Lay her down!
Come on!

1257
02:03:41,027 --> 02:03:43,607
Come on!
Slowly! Slowly!

1258
02:03:48,973 --> 02:03:53,433
I will be waiting for you on the way to
Söğüt.

1259
02:03:55,227 --> 02:03:56,737
Come on!

1260
02:04:04,624 --> 02:04:05,894
Soldiers.

1261
02:04:06,358 --> 02:04:07,688
Get ready!

1262
02:04:09,241 --> 02:04:11,241
Vizier Alemşah.

1263
02:04:12,295 --> 02:04:16,725
He disobeyed your order an tried to hang
me in Bilecik.

1264
02:04:18,318 --> 02:04:20,988
Sergeant İlgezdi stopped it.

1265
02:04:22,587 --> 02:04:26,517
Since he knew I would come here and
tell you all the truth...

1266
02:04:28,058 --> 02:04:30,248
...he sent Geyhatu at me.

1267
02:04:32,333 --> 02:04:36,093
These are very serious accusations,
Osman Bey.

1268
02:04:37,172 --> 02:04:39,992
He made my brother turn his back on me.

1269
02:04:40,663 --> 02:04:43,083
He put Sheik Edebalı in a dungeon.

1270
02:04:44,574 --> 02:04:49,404
He is trying to get everyone on his side
by working with the Lords.

1271
02:04:50,962 --> 02:04:52,862
Thus...

1272
02:04:55,426 --> 02:04:57,926
...he had to dismiss me.

1273
02:05:02,222 --> 02:05:03,792
If you don't have proof...

1274
02:05:04,774 --> 02:05:07,264
...these words are just slanders.

1275
02:05:09,067 --> 02:05:10,847
Did you appoint...

1276
02:05:12,731 --> 02:05:15,121
...the Vizier there?

1277
02:05:15,593 --> 02:05:17,773
What is it, Osman?

1278
02:05:18,714 --> 02:05:21,744
Are you questioning our power?

1279
02:05:23,532 --> 02:05:25,482
Of course, I did!

1280
02:05:25,926 --> 02:05:27,856
I would never disrespect you, my Sultan.

1281
02:05:35,177 --> 02:05:37,977
Alemşah always said...

1282
02:05:38,535 --> 02:05:41,775
...those lands needed order.

1283
02:05:46,869 --> 02:05:51,849
It is easy to subdue both the Mongols
and the Rums, he said.

1284
02:05:55,513 --> 02:05:57,763
He always wanted to be there.

1285
02:05:59,639 --> 02:06:01,589
What does this prove?

1286
02:06:04,040 --> 02:06:08,640
Everyone thinks positively of the matters
on these lands except you.

1287
02:06:09,523 --> 02:06:12,543
Tell me, do you have proof?

1288
02:06:13,413 --> 02:06:14,906
Proof?

1289
02:06:19,642 --> 02:06:21,282
Proof...

1290
02:06:22,659 --> 02:06:24,939
...is what I see with my eyes...

1291
02:06:25,743 --> 02:06:27,723
...what I believe with my heart...

1292
02:06:29,054 --> 02:06:31,694
...what I say with my mouth, my Sultan.

1293
02:06:33,197 --> 02:06:37,827
It is your choice to believe it or not.

1294
02:06:41,523 --> 02:06:43,123
But...

1295
02:06:44,660 --> 02:06:46,850
...when he uses the power he gained...

1296
02:06:47,450 --> 02:06:49,470
...against you...

1297
02:06:51,856 --> 02:06:55,306
...you will understand that my words
are true.

1298
02:06:59,970 --> 02:07:02,910
I obey whatever the Sultan's order is.

1299
02:07:05,796 --> 02:07:07,716
Order, my Sultan.

1300
02:07:16,875 --> 02:07:18,445
Are you all right, my girl?

1301
02:07:18,960 --> 02:07:21,510
I am, mother. I can manage until
the village.

1302
02:07:21,957 --> 02:07:24,837
He will be so mischievous.

1303
02:07:27,617 --> 02:07:30,732
We must get to the village soon. He is
obviously coming early.

1304
02:07:30,732 --> 02:07:32,902
-Yes, mother.
-Alps!

1305
02:07:33,347 --> 02:07:34,507
To the horses!

1306
02:07:34,507 --> 02:07:35,897
Come on.

1307
02:07:37,396 --> 02:07:38,916
Come on.

1308
02:07:40,473 --> 02:07:42,163
Bala, stop!

1309
02:07:54,012 --> 02:07:56,162
My Allah, protect my child.

1310
02:07:59,352 --> 02:08:01,022
Bala!

1311
02:08:03,188 --> 02:08:04,498
Bala!

1312
02:08:10,725 --> 02:08:12,895
I told you I will kill you!

1313
02:08:14,154 --> 02:08:15,854
Here I am.

1314
02:08:17,007 --> 02:08:19,407
I don't like unfinished businesses.

1315
02:08:19,935 --> 02:08:24,735
I will kill you and the one inside you!

1316
02:08:27,223 --> 02:08:29,454
Let's see you dog!

1317
02:08:29,454 --> 02:08:31,924
-Attack!
-Zehra, protect Bala!

1318
02:08:32,203 --> 02:08:33,518
Protect Bala!

1319
02:08:33,518 --> 02:08:34,778
Julia!

1320
02:08:41,910 --> 02:08:45,040
My Allah, please protect my child!

1321
02:08:45,434 --> 02:08:47,744
Alps, protect Bala!

1322
02:09:29,513 --> 02:09:31,133
Bala!

1323
02:09:42,034 --> 02:09:43,664
Bala!

1324
02:09:57,121 --> 02:09:58,581
Die!

1325
02:10:09,227 --> 02:10:10,687
Mother!

1326
02:10:12,455 --> 02:10:14,025
Mother!

1327
02:10:20,608 --> 02:10:22,608
-Mother!
-Mother!

1328
02:10:35,317 --> 02:10:37,577
Mother! Mother!
Don't! No!

1329
02:10:38,501 --> 02:10:39,771
Mother! No!

1330
02:10:39,833 --> 02:10:42,103
I've known you for a long time.

1331
02:10:42,292 --> 02:10:44,882
I know you have good intentions.

1332
02:10:47,563 --> 02:10:50,313
But I fear that...

1333
02:10:51,482 --> 02:10:55,302
... the strength of your wrist,
the courage of your heart...

1334
02:10:56,619 --> 02:10:59,069
...may blind you.

1335
02:11:04,297 --> 02:11:08,307
What about the letter that came from
Alemşah?

1336
02:11:12,101 --> 02:11:15,011
That you had the intention of
forming a state--

1337
02:11:16,699 --> 02:11:18,889
You dog!

1338
02:11:25,580 --> 02:11:29,120
I will kill you,
with the order of Geyhatu, Osman.

1339
02:11:40,595 --> 02:11:42,395
My Sultan!

1340
02:11:42,420 --> 02:11:43,680
My Sultan!

1341
02:11:43,796 --> 02:11:45,486
My Sultan!

1342
02:12:03,269 --> 02:12:05,629
You vile dog!

1343
02:12:34,999 --> 02:12:37,309
My Allah...

1344
02:12:38,929 --> 02:12:41,739
...who gives the best of all.

1345
02:12:49,108 --> 02:12:51,158
Help me get out of this...

1346
02:12:52,150 --> 02:12:56,200
...with my head up.

1347
02:13:06,562 --> 02:13:15,662
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com